1
00:00:14,252 --> 00:00:16,244
[music: "My Bias, My Boss" theme song]

2
00:00:52,005 --> 00:00:52,812
(This drama is a work of fiction)

3
00:00:52,836 --> 00:00:54,105
(Any similarity to real people,
organizations, or events is coincidental)

4
00:00:55,339 --> 00:00:56,863
[faint dog barking]

5
00:00:58,750 --> 00:01:00,232
[cheerful music]

6
00:01:07,272 --> 00:01:09,272
(Dareum) He seems completely unfazed.

7
00:01:09,339 --> 00:01:10,472
[whoosh sound]

8
00:01:11,238 --> 00:01:12,372
[Dareum gasps]

9
00:01:13,011 --> 00:01:14,673
[pants]

10
00:01:16,672 --> 00:01:19,017
That was like a car accident.

11
00:01:19,084 --> 00:01:20,420
(Hagi) I mean...

12
00:01:20,487 --> 00:01:21,987
It was a minor accident.

13
00:01:22,054 --> 00:01:22,848
[laughs]

14
00:01:22,915 --> 00:01:24,122
Right. A minor accident.

15
00:01:24,728 --> 00:01:27,192
(Dareum) Right.

16
00:01:27,259 --> 00:01:29,220
I was just trying to catch this.

17
00:01:29,287 --> 00:01:31,041
The wind suddenly blew it away...

18
00:01:31,108 --> 00:01:33,164
[laughs awkwardly]
Yeah.

19
00:01:33,231 --> 00:01:35,906
Why did this have to fly away like that?

20
00:01:36,435 --> 00:01:37,405
[exhales]

21
00:01:37,472 --> 00:01:38,639
[whoosh sound]

22
00:01:38,706 --> 00:01:41,406
(Dareum) Unlike me,
I'm sure he's dated people before.
[music stops]

23
00:01:43,539 --> 00:01:44,539
(Hagi) I...

24
00:01:46,676 --> 00:01:48,579
Get home safely, then.

25
00:01:48,646 --> 00:01:51,116
You too, Mr. Kang.

26
00:01:53,189 --> 00:01:55,754
Thank you for today.

27
00:01:57,322 --> 00:01:58,256
(Hagi) Bye, then.

28
00:02:04,292 --> 00:02:05,384
[footsteps fading]

29
00:02:05,451 --> 00:02:06,732
(Dareum) Am I the only one
affected by that?

30
00:02:08,366 --> 00:02:09,892
[spraying]

31
00:02:09,959 --> 00:02:10,984
[lid clicks]

32
00:02:13,572 --> 00:02:15,607
(Hagi) That was like a car accident.
[cheerful music]

33
00:02:15,674 --> 00:02:17,343
[heart beating sound]
I mean...

34
00:02:17,410 --> 00:02:18,872
It was a minor accident.

35
00:02:19,544 --> 00:02:20,605
A minor accident.

36
00:02:20,672 --> 00:02:22,138
[whoosh sound]
[music stops]

37
00:02:22,885 --> 00:02:23,915
That...

38
00:02:24,646 --> 00:02:25,784
was my first kiss...

39
00:02:27,048 --> 00:02:28,653
[taps]
Jeez.
[cheerful music continues]

40
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:30,872
How is he so unfazed?

41
00:02:31,722 --> 00:02:33,203
Is he a player or what?

42
00:02:33,759 --> 00:02:35,274
[sighs]
[heart beating sound]

43
00:02:37,262 --> 00:02:38,296
[grunts]

44
00:02:39,498 --> 00:02:42,073
(Dareum) But why
is my heart beating so fast?
[heartbeat sound continues]

45
00:02:43,903 --> 00:02:45,370
[sighs]
[music stops]

46
00:02:45,437 --> 00:02:46,726
[phone vibrating]
[gasps]

47
00:02:49,574 --> 00:02:51,810
[message notification sound]
(Lee Chan) Dareum,
did you get home safely?

48
00:02:55,699 --> 00:02:56,746
[phone clacks]

49
00:02:57,109 --> 00:02:58,259
[sighs]

50
00:03:00,147 --> 00:03:01,508
[exhales]

51
00:03:01,806 --> 00:03:03,205
What's wrong with me?

52
00:03:04,485 --> 00:03:06,327
[street sounds]
[door opens]

53
00:03:06,394 --> 00:03:09,171
(Episode 7)
- (Yeongwoo) A friend...
- (Mina) Oh...

54
00:03:09,238 --> 00:03:11,296
[Dareum yawns]
[Mina laughs]

55
00:03:11,363 --> 00:03:13,531
Did you not get enough sleep last night?

56
00:03:13,598 --> 00:03:15,872
- (Yeongwoo) You look a bit tired.
- (Mina) Yeah.
[Dareum laughs]

57
00:03:15,939 --> 00:03:17,339
Well...

58
00:03:17,406 --> 00:03:19,145
I couldn't sleep a wink.

59
00:03:19,212 --> 00:03:21,639
(Mina) Why couldn't you sleep a wink?

60
00:03:21,706 --> 00:03:23,522
(Yeongwoo) There are days like that.
[Mina reacts]

61
00:03:23,589 --> 00:03:25,739
[yawns]

62
00:03:25,806 --> 00:03:27,045
[elevator dings]

63
00:03:27,112 --> 00:03:28,694
[sniffles]
[Dareum grunts]
[Mina reacts]

64
00:03:29,781 --> 00:03:31,171
(Yeongwoo) Hello.

65
00:03:31,238 --> 00:03:33,284
I'll go to the corner...
[employees greeting each other]

66
00:03:33,351 --> 00:03:35,038
(Dareum, Mina) Excuse me.

67
00:03:35,105 --> 00:03:36,739
- (automated voice) Doors closing.
- (Dareum) Sorry.

68
00:03:39,351 --> 00:03:40,492
[elevator doors close]

69
00:03:45,162 --> 00:03:46,437
[Dareum gasps]
[intriguing music]

70
00:03:46,504 --> 00:03:48,440
[Dareum grunts]

71
00:03:49,234 --> 00:03:51,352
[thud sound]
[employees gasp]
I'm sorry...

72
00:03:53,776 --> 00:03:55,605
[thud sound]
[employees gasp]
(Yeongwoo) What is it?

73
00:03:55,672 --> 00:03:57,403
- (Dareum) Sorry...
- (Mina) Oh, gosh.
[music stops]

74
00:03:58,222 --> 00:04:00,712
I'll move to this side...

75
00:04:00,779 --> 00:04:02,247
[upbeat music]

76
00:04:02,314 --> 00:04:04,216
- (Hagi) Excuse me.
- (Dareum) Sorry.

77
00:04:04,283 --> 00:04:05,539
(Hagi) Just a moment.

78
00:04:06,551 --> 00:04:07,672
[comical sound]

79
00:04:08,172 --> 00:04:09,420
[Mina grunts]

80
00:04:09,487 --> 00:04:11,242
(Mina) Mr. Kang!

81
00:04:11,309 --> 00:04:13,292
There's someone right here, sir.

82
00:04:13,359 --> 00:04:15,327
[comical sound]
Mr. Kang, I'm standing right here.

83
00:04:15,394 --> 00:04:17,762
It's me, Mina. Lee Mina!
[ding sound]

84
00:04:18,397 --> 00:04:19,431
[Mina grunts]

85
00:04:19,965 --> 00:04:21,138
[Dareum sighs]

86
00:04:21,205 --> 00:04:22,300
(Dareum) Am I...

87
00:04:23,253 --> 00:04:25,070
the only one who feels embarrassed?
[music stops]

88
00:04:25,137 --> 00:04:27,272
(Mina) Can he not see me?
[squeaking sound]

89
00:04:29,197 --> 00:04:30,975
[cat meowing sound]

90
00:04:32,177 --> 00:04:33,827
[squeaking sound]
[intriguing music]

91
00:04:35,447 --> 00:04:37,205
[cat meowing sound]

92
00:04:38,850 --> 00:04:39,964
[comical sound]

93
00:04:40,031 --> 00:04:41,354
[cat meowing sound]

94
00:04:42,279 --> 00:04:43,588
[cat meowing sound]

95
00:04:43,655 --> 00:04:44,951
[comical sound]

96
00:04:45,639 --> 00:04:46,839
[cat meowing sound]

97
00:04:46,906 --> 00:04:48,039
[comical sound]

98
00:04:51,830 --> 00:04:52,872
[music stops]

99
00:04:53,809 --> 00:04:55,007
(Chandong) Mr. Lee.

100
00:04:55,074 --> 00:04:56,881
Thank you for deciding so quickly.

101
00:04:56,948 --> 00:04:58,244
(Lee Chan) Not at all.

102
00:04:58,311 --> 00:05:00,205
I could hardly sleep
after receiving the offer yesterday.

103
00:05:00,933 --> 00:05:04,009
It's been a long-time dream of mine
to work with you, Director.
[Wonbin, PD laugh]

104
00:05:04,076 --> 00:05:05,310
(Chandong) Then...

105
00:05:05,914 --> 00:05:08,247
I'll discuss it with
our US co-production partner

106
00:05:08,271 --> 00:05:09,380
and get back to you.

107
00:05:09,447 --> 00:05:11,261
There probably won't be any major issues.

108
00:05:11,328 --> 00:05:14,678
(Lee Chan) If you give me
the opportunity, I'll do my best.

109
00:05:14,745 --> 00:05:17,569
(PD) Well, it's going to be shot
entirely on location in LA.

110
00:05:17,636 --> 00:05:19,205
Check this here.

111
00:05:19,824 --> 00:05:21,905
Once you're officially cast,

112
00:05:21,972 --> 00:05:24,180
why don't you come early
to get accustomed to the location?

113
00:05:24,247 --> 00:05:26,022
They've already booked a villa there.

114
00:05:26,089 --> 00:05:28,195
(Chandong) You can get some rest there
like you're on vacation,

115
00:05:28,262 --> 00:05:30,472
and join us for meetings or table reads.

116
00:05:30,539 --> 00:05:31,369
[exhales]

117
00:05:31,436 --> 00:05:32,865
(Wonbin) I think it's a great idea.

118
00:05:32,889 --> 00:05:33,973
You could get adjusted
to the time difference.

119
00:05:35,583 --> 00:05:37,675
Yes, that sounds great.
[Chandong laughs]

120
00:05:37,742 --> 00:05:38,710
[PD reacts]

121
00:05:40,879 --> 00:05:41,939
[Wonbin sighs]

122
00:05:42,314 --> 00:05:43,182
[Wonbin exclaims]

123
00:05:43,206 --> 00:05:45,839
(Wonbin) Chan. At this point,
you've got the role
[button clicks]

124
00:05:46,890 --> 00:05:48,006
Congratulations.

125
00:05:48,073 --> 00:05:49,268
[clasping hands]
[Wonbin laughs]

126
00:05:49,335 --> 00:05:52,876
You've always wanted to go to Hollywood.
Your dream's finally coming true.

127
00:05:52,943 --> 00:05:55,254
(Lee Chan) It's all thanks to you.
[Wonbin laughs]

128
00:05:55,321 --> 00:05:58,530
(Wonbin) We should sort out
your schedule in Korea first.

129
00:05:58,597 --> 00:06:00,086
[rustles]

130
00:06:02,033 --> 00:06:03,849
(Lee Chan) Will I be in the States
for a long time?

131
00:06:03,916 --> 00:06:05,971
Well, yeah. It'll be shot entirely in LA.

132
00:06:06,705 --> 00:06:09,372
(Wonbin) But this could really
make your career.

133
00:06:15,205 --> 00:06:17,205
(Dareum
Yes, I got home safely! Get some rest!)

134
00:06:17,230 --> 00:06:18,213
[rustles]

135
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:19,610
[Wonbin sighs]

136
00:06:21,031 --> 00:06:22,220
Are you dating, by any chance?

137
00:06:25,839 --> 00:06:27,058
[Lee Chan scoffs]
Chan.

138
00:06:27,125 --> 00:06:29,305
You've had paparazzi on your tail
these past few days,

139
00:06:30,656 --> 00:06:31,954
and this is a crucial time for you.

140
00:06:32,021 --> 00:06:33,305
[elevator dings]

141
00:06:34,066 --> 00:06:35,639
[elevator doors opening]
[taps]

142
00:06:38,236 --> 00:06:39,471
[button clicks]

143
00:06:39,538 --> 00:06:40,739
I know that too...

144
00:06:42,973 --> 00:06:44,342
[announcement plays]

145
00:06:45,155 --> 00:06:46,833
[announcement plays]
[Dareum gasps]

146
00:06:53,075 --> 00:06:54,719
[Dareum, Hagi gasp]
[intriguing music]

147
00:06:54,786 --> 00:06:56,688
Mr. Kang.
[laughs]

148
00:06:56,755 --> 00:06:58,017
[Hagi reacts]
[clears throat]

149
00:06:58,084 --> 00:06:59,545
Ms. Nam.
[Dareum reacts]

150
00:06:59,612 --> 00:07:01,994
You must be here to buy stuff for Koong.

151
00:07:02,061 --> 00:07:03,105
(Hagi) Yes.

152
00:07:03,702 --> 00:07:04,896
Does Jjak like this too?

153
00:07:04,963 --> 00:07:06,431
(Dareum) Yes, totally.

154
00:07:06,498 --> 00:07:08,666
The moment I hold this,
Jjak suddenly turns into a predator.

155
00:07:08,733 --> 00:07:10,235
[Hagi scoffs]
[Dareum laughs awkwardly]

156
00:07:10,302 --> 00:07:12,372
Then I should get one of each.
[Dareum reacts]
[music stops]

157
00:07:14,406 --> 00:07:16,408
[thuds]
I see you're not working late today.

158
00:07:16,475 --> 00:07:17,942
(Hagi) I usually work at home these days.

159
00:07:18,009 --> 00:07:19,501
I feel like Koong waits for me all day.

160
00:07:19,568 --> 00:07:21,372
I do too...
[laughs awkwardly]

161
00:07:23,867 --> 00:07:26,054
(Hagi) Then should we meet up sometime?

162
00:07:26,121 --> 00:07:27,194
[reacts]

163
00:07:27,261 --> 00:07:28,198
[ding sound]
(Dareum) What?

164
00:07:28,265 --> 00:07:30,055
[dramatic sound]
[intriguing music]

165
00:07:30,122 --> 00:07:31,039
(Hagi) Oh...

166
00:07:31,589 --> 00:07:32,657
I mean...

167
00:07:33,058 --> 00:07:34,325
Well...

168
00:07:35,027 --> 00:07:36,672
I meant Koong and Jjak.

169
00:07:37,762 --> 00:07:39,030
We should let them play together.

170
00:07:39,518 --> 00:07:40,999
[Dareum reacts]

171
00:07:41,066 --> 00:07:42,133
Right.

172
00:07:45,205 --> 00:07:46,371
He startled me.

173
00:07:49,138 --> 00:07:50,006
[thud sound]

174
00:07:50,073 --> 00:07:51,588
[bright music]

175
00:08:01,566 --> 00:08:03,339
[exciting sound]

176
00:08:09,238 --> 00:08:10,370
[thuds]

177
00:08:11,263 --> 00:08:12,255
Gosh.

178
00:08:12,965 --> 00:08:14,532
So I wasn't the only one who was affected.

179
00:08:17,135 --> 00:08:20,272
[phone vibrating]
[music stops]

180
00:08:21,719 --> 00:08:23,319
(Chan)

181
00:08:24,744 --> 00:08:26,705
(Dareum) Let me take this.

182
00:08:26,772 --> 00:08:27,846
(Hagi) Sure.

183
00:08:28,539 --> 00:08:30,839
[vibration continues]

184
00:08:34,455 --> 00:08:35,619
[phone clacks]

185
00:08:37,122 --> 00:08:38,856
Hi.
[intriguing music]
[thud sound]

186
00:08:38,923 --> 00:08:40,358
[flinching sound]

187
00:08:40,425 --> 00:08:43,808
(Dareum) I was going to call you
when I got home...
[music stops]

188
00:08:45,066 --> 00:08:46,880
[laughs awkwardly]
No...

189
00:08:46,947 --> 00:08:49,067
I'm fine.

190
00:08:49,134 --> 00:08:50,034
[calm music]

191
00:08:50,101 --> 00:08:52,156
Yes, I got home safely last night.

192
00:08:52,945 --> 00:08:55,373
What happened to that urgent business?

193
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:57,508
(Lee Chan) It went well.
Thanks for asking.

194
00:08:57,575 --> 00:08:59,439
That's a relief.

195
00:08:59,944 --> 00:09:02,908
(Lee Chan) Dareum, there's something
I really want to say to you.

196
00:09:02,975 --> 00:09:04,415
Do you have time tomorrow evening?

197
00:09:04,482 --> 00:09:07,185
I'll send you the address.
Let's meet after work.

198
00:09:08,142 --> 00:09:09,606
[exhales]
Okay.

199
00:09:12,627 --> 00:09:13,580
(Lee Chan) And...

200
00:09:13,647 --> 00:09:16,243
Can I call you back later?

201
00:09:16,310 --> 00:09:17,839
- (Lee Chan) Sure. Okay.
- (Dareum) Bye.

202
00:09:19,497 --> 00:09:20,385
[call ending sound]

203
00:09:20,452 --> 00:09:22,458
Sorry about that.

204
00:09:22,525 --> 00:09:24,105
(Hagi) It's fine.
[music stops]

205
00:09:29,761 --> 00:09:30,863
(Hagi) Was that...

206
00:09:31,843 --> 00:09:32,973
the man...

207
00:09:33,779 --> 00:09:34,746
from the blind date?

208
00:09:35,435 --> 00:09:36,281
(Dareum) What?

209
00:09:37,628 --> 00:09:38,950
[laughs awkwardly]
Yes.

210
00:09:40,826 --> 00:09:42,372
(Hagi) He contacted you again
after leaving like that?

211
00:09:43,685 --> 00:09:45,000
(Dareum) Oh...

212
00:09:46,142 --> 00:09:47,405
I guess he felt bad.

213
00:09:47,893 --> 00:09:48,968
[sighs]

214
00:09:50,038 --> 00:09:52,297
He shouldn't have left you like that
if he was going to feel bad.

215
00:09:53,361 --> 00:09:54,832
It's not like he's some celebrity
or something.

216
00:09:55,233 --> 00:09:57,001
[flinching sound]
(Hagi) How busy could he possibly be?

217
00:09:58,559 --> 00:10:00,505
[laughs awkwardly]

218
00:10:01,710 --> 00:10:03,675
Right...

219
00:10:05,110 --> 00:10:06,344
(Hagi) Ms. Nam, do you know

220
00:10:07,331 --> 00:10:09,339
that you said you were fine just now too?

221
00:10:11,837 --> 00:10:13,077
[sighs]

222
00:10:14,507 --> 00:10:15,820
Did I...
[laughs awkwardly]

223
00:10:16,488 --> 00:10:17,559
say that again?

224
00:10:18,949 --> 00:10:20,525
(Hagi) No matter
what kind of person he is,

225
00:10:21,582 --> 00:10:23,795
there's no reason for you
to bend over backwards for him.

226
00:10:25,158 --> 00:10:26,868
[soft music]

227
00:10:29,234 --> 00:10:30,268
[faint laugh]

228
00:10:33,627 --> 00:10:34,737
You're right.

229
00:10:36,563 --> 00:10:37,678
(Dareum) To tell you the truth,

230
00:10:38,685 --> 00:10:39,844
it wasn't a blind date.

231
00:10:40,746 --> 00:10:43,648
He's someone I've liked from afar
for a long time.

232
00:10:49,841 --> 00:10:50,839
But...

233
00:10:51,690 --> 00:10:53,258
once I started seeing him...

234
00:10:56,395 --> 00:10:57,428
[sighs]

235
00:10:58,090 --> 00:10:59,864
I found myself trying to accommodate him

236
00:11:00,769 --> 00:11:02,600
when he didn't even ask me to.

237
00:11:03,835 --> 00:11:05,271
I always

238
00:11:05,338 --> 00:11:07,138
prioritized him before myself,

239
00:11:07,873 --> 00:11:09,807
and my feelings came second.

240
00:11:14,072 --> 00:11:15,327
[deep sigh]

241
00:11:16,137 --> 00:11:17,148
So I actually...

242
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:19,639
feel a bit confused.

243
00:11:25,446 --> 00:11:26,906
(Hagi) Then just set one rule.

244
00:11:28,794 --> 00:11:29,739
Think about...

245
00:11:32,064 --> 00:11:34,432
whether he makes you more like yourself,

246
00:11:36,090 --> 00:11:37,074
or...

247
00:11:38,070 --> 00:11:39,470
makes you feel smaller.

248
00:11:44,276 --> 00:11:45,710
Whatever you decide,

249
00:11:46,472 --> 00:11:48,179
just think about whether it's a choice

250
00:11:49,548 --> 00:11:50,548
true to you.

251
00:11:55,151 --> 00:11:56,490
[music stops]

252
00:12:00,592 --> 00:12:03,127
[beeps]
- (automated voice) Payment completed.
- (employee) Here you go.

253
00:12:04,898 --> 00:12:05,863
[grabs bottle]

254
00:12:05,930 --> 00:12:07,310
[street noise]

255
00:12:12,903 --> 00:12:14,052
[lid clicks]

256
00:12:16,939 --> 00:12:18,242
(Dareum) It wasn't a blind date.
[whoosh sound]

257
00:12:18,309 --> 00:12:19,786
He's someone

258
00:12:20,410 --> 00:12:22,438
I've liked from afar for a long time.
[whoosh sound]

259
00:12:22,505 --> 00:12:23,283
[spits]

260
00:12:23,350 --> 00:12:25,455
[somber music]
[coughs]

261
00:12:27,044 --> 00:12:28,782
[comical sound]
He's someone

262
00:12:28,849 --> 00:12:29,703
[deep sigh]

263
00:12:29,770 --> 00:12:32,057
I've liked from afar for a long time.
[bubble popping sound]

264
00:12:32,124 --> 00:12:33,453
Liked from afar...

265
00:12:34,957 --> 00:12:36,127
for a long time...

266
00:12:37,143 --> 00:12:38,329
It wasn't me.

267
00:12:40,605 --> 00:12:42,177
It wasn't me...

268
00:12:42,968 --> 00:12:44,240
[laughs]

269
00:12:44,307 --> 00:12:46,339
(Dareum) I'll give it a try.

270
00:12:46,871 --> 00:12:49,006
[sparkling sound]
[music stops]

271
00:12:49,073 --> 00:12:51,676
I'll be more like myself.

272
00:12:53,516 --> 00:12:55,646
I really like you.

273
00:12:56,265 --> 00:12:58,730
[voice echoing] I really like you.
[passionate music]

274
00:12:59,284 --> 00:13:00,485
[laughs]

275
00:13:01,272 --> 00:13:02,982
[sparkling sound]

276
00:13:03,843 --> 00:13:05,556
(Hagi) This is so annoying.

277
00:13:07,793 --> 00:13:09,006
Darn it...

278
00:13:10,027 --> 00:13:10,891
[music stops]

279
00:13:10,958 --> 00:13:12,439
Who the hell is he?

280
00:13:13,464 --> 00:13:14,939
[tapping keyboard]

281
00:13:18,805 --> 00:13:20,605
(Welcome, Hagi
What can I help you with today?)

282
00:13:23,417 --> 00:13:24,643
[scoffs]

283
00:13:24,710 --> 00:13:26,277
[intriguing music]

284
00:13:26,674 --> 00:13:27,912
[tapping keyboard]

285
00:13:27,936 --> 00:13:29,936
(Disappointed after meeting
someone you've liked)

286
00:13:31,783 --> 00:13:32,850
[beep sound]

287
00:13:34,452 --> 00:13:35,974
- (Luni) Hello!
- Oh, my gosh!
[music stops]

288
00:13:36,041 --> 00:13:37,891
(Luni) Would you like me to share

289
00:13:37,958 --> 00:13:40,572
some helpful information
about your search?
[comical sound]

290
00:13:41,158 --> 00:13:42,293
[sighs]

291
00:13:47,256 --> 00:13:49,272
[whoosh sound]
[cheerful music]

292
00:13:50,843 --> 00:13:51,769
(Hagi) Well...

293
00:13:52,604 --> 00:13:53,939
Go on, then.

294
00:13:54,006 --> 00:13:57,432
(Luni) It's common to feel disappointed
when you finally meet someone

295
00:13:57,499 --> 00:14:00,739
you've idealized for a long time.

296
00:14:00,806 --> 00:14:03,709
It's a feeling that comes from the gap
between expectations and reality.
[whoosh sound]

297
00:14:03,776 --> 00:14:04,875
Right?

298
00:14:06,339 --> 00:14:09,420
You should date someone who likes you
instead of clinging to a crush.

299
00:14:09,487 --> 00:14:10,187
Don't you think?

300
00:14:10,254 --> 00:14:11,155
(Luni) Statistically,

301
00:14:11,222 --> 00:14:12,892
stable romantic relationships
[swish sound]

302
00:14:12,959 --> 00:14:15,941
are more likely to develop
with someone close

303
00:14:16,008 --> 00:14:18,560
who expresses their interest first
instead of someone

304
00:14:18,627 --> 00:14:20,906
you've had a one-sided crush on
for a long time.

305
00:14:24,805 --> 00:14:25,903
"Someone close"?

306
00:14:26,505 --> 00:14:27,839
[sparkling sound]
(Luni) Someone close.

307
00:14:31,033 --> 00:14:32,042
[music stops]

308
00:14:32,109 --> 00:14:33,588
[street sounds]

309
00:14:43,573 --> 00:14:44,939
[paper rustling]

310
00:14:51,262 --> 00:14:52,372
You did a great job.

311
00:14:52,828 --> 00:14:53,831
(Hagi) Let's proceed with this.

312
00:14:54,272 --> 00:14:55,733
[laughs]

313
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:58,469
(Dareum) Okay. I'll do my best
with the preparations.

314
00:15:01,231 --> 00:15:02,273
Ms. Nam.

315
00:15:03,458 --> 00:15:04,375
(Dareum) Yes?

316
00:15:05,344 --> 00:15:06,511
What are you doing this evening?

317
00:15:08,098 --> 00:15:09,080
(Dareum) Excuse me?

318
00:15:09,875 --> 00:15:11,414
(Hagi) Oh...
[cheerful music]

319
00:15:11,481 --> 00:15:12,750
I mean...

320
00:15:13,416 --> 00:15:16,254
Let's meet...

321
00:15:17,055 --> 00:15:18,322
with Koong and Jjak.

322
00:15:19,040 --> 00:15:20,191
Right!

323
00:15:20,792 --> 00:15:23,606
But I actually have plans today.

324
00:15:24,763 --> 00:15:25,739
[reacts]

325
00:15:26,465 --> 00:15:28,772
Then let me know when you're free.

326
00:15:29,835 --> 00:15:30,839
Yes, Mr. Kang.

327
00:15:40,412 --> 00:15:41,557
[door closes]

328
00:15:42,463 --> 00:15:43,405
Plans?

329
00:15:43,472 --> 00:15:44,418
[intriguing music]
[thud sound]

330
00:15:44,485 --> 00:15:46,138
(Hagi) She has plans?

331
00:15:50,768 --> 00:15:53,106
Could she be meeting that guy?

332
00:15:53,173 --> 00:15:55,334
[comical sound]
(Dareum) Can I call you back later?

333
00:15:55,401 --> 00:15:56,660
[bubble popping sound]

334
00:15:56,727 --> 00:15:57,928
[Hagi laughs]
[tapping sound]

335
00:15:57,995 --> 00:15:59,599
No way.

336
00:15:59,666 --> 00:16:01,150
It can't be.

337
00:16:05,654 --> 00:16:06,973
[music stops]

338
00:16:11,008 --> 00:16:11,882
[door opens]

339
00:16:11,949 --> 00:16:14,059
(employee) Hello. Come inside, ma'am.

340
00:16:14,126 --> 00:16:15,839
[elegant music plays]
(Dareum) Okay.

341
00:16:19,728 --> 00:16:20,772
[door closes]

342
00:16:22,495 --> 00:16:24,006
[rattling]

343
00:16:29,662 --> 00:16:30,748
Sir.

344
00:16:32,367 --> 00:16:33,564
[Dareum laughs]

345
00:16:33,631 --> 00:16:35,242
- You're here.
- (Dareum) Yes.

346
00:16:35,309 --> 00:16:37,039
(employee) Let me know
if you need anything.

347
00:16:37,866 --> 00:16:39,070
(Dareum) Thank you.

348
00:16:40,806 --> 00:16:42,373
But why are we...

349
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:43,651
[inhales]

350
00:16:43,718 --> 00:16:45,138
I have something to celebrate.

351
00:16:45,950 --> 00:16:47,562
(Lee Chan) So I wanted to do
some shopping quietly

352
00:16:47,629 --> 00:16:48,879
and enjoy a date with you.

353
00:16:50,215 --> 00:16:51,706
[Lee Chan, Dareum laugh]

354
00:16:52,317 --> 00:16:53,217
Right!

355
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:57,895
Do you want to try this on?

356
00:16:57,962 --> 00:16:58,864
This?

357
00:16:58,931 --> 00:17:00,305
I think it'll suit you.

358
00:17:02,707 --> 00:17:04,462
[Dareum laughs]

359
00:17:05,234 --> 00:17:06,405
(Dareum) It's pretty.

360
00:17:06,832 --> 00:17:07,832
[faint laugh]

361
00:17:13,905 --> 00:17:14,906
[laughs awkwardly]

362
00:17:20,045 --> 00:17:21,105
[laughs awkwardly]

363
00:17:21,739 --> 00:17:22,605
[Dareum grunts]

364
00:17:22,672 --> 00:17:23,648
(Dareum) Do I look okay?

365
00:17:24,525 --> 00:17:26,317
Yeah. You look great.

366
00:17:26,384 --> 00:17:28,839
[Dareum reacts]
(employee) Neutral tones really suit you.

367
00:17:28,906 --> 00:17:30,138
[Dareum laughs awkwardly]

368
00:17:30,997 --> 00:17:32,138
(Lee Chan) It looks great on you.

369
00:17:32,205 --> 00:17:33,290
[Dareum laughs awkwardly]

370
00:17:35,027 --> 00:17:36,060
Try this on too.

371
00:17:36,627 --> 00:17:39,496
I really don't think this will suit me.

372
00:17:39,563 --> 00:17:41,165
It'll look different once you try it on.

373
00:17:42,426 --> 00:17:43,434
[grunts]

374
00:17:44,228 --> 00:17:46,026
[Dareum laughs awkwardly]
[uplifting music]

375
00:17:48,073 --> 00:17:49,473
[grunts]

376
00:17:52,311 --> 00:17:53,377
[grunts]

377
00:17:54,279 --> 00:17:55,505
[grunts]
[laughs awkwardly]

378
00:18:01,352 --> 00:18:02,572
[faint laugh]

379
00:18:04,956 --> 00:18:05,990
[door closes]

380
00:18:09,661 --> 00:18:10,394
[exclaims]

381
00:18:10,461 --> 00:18:12,096
(Dareum) I look weird, don't I?

382
00:18:12,163 --> 00:18:13,564
(Lee Chan) Not at all.

383
00:18:13,631 --> 00:18:14,720
You look so pretty.

384
00:18:14,787 --> 00:18:15,973
[exhales]

385
00:18:16,535 --> 00:18:18,505
I don't usually...

386
00:18:18,572 --> 00:18:20,539
wear clothes like this.

387
00:18:20,606 --> 00:18:21,972
That's why I like it even more.

388
00:18:22,608 --> 00:18:24,875
(Lee Chan) I'm surprised
at how this look suits you too.

389
00:18:25,410 --> 00:18:26,965
[laughs awkwardly]

390
00:18:27,032 --> 00:18:28,612
Dareum, just a moment.

391
00:18:39,082 --> 00:18:40,739
[Dareum laughs awkwardly]
[Lee Chan laughs]

392
00:18:43,677 --> 00:18:45,362
(Lee Chan) You could wear this
when we go to LA.

393
00:18:47,177 --> 00:18:48,299
(Dareum) LA?

394
00:18:49,629 --> 00:18:51,330
(Lee Chan) Yes.
[music fades]

395
00:18:51,397 --> 00:18:54,400
(Dareum) Then it's almost confirmed.

396
00:18:54,467 --> 00:18:57,615
Wow. You're working
with Director Park Chandong.
[elegant music plays]

397
00:18:58,706 --> 00:19:00,772
That's so cool.
[laughs]

398
00:19:00,839 --> 00:19:02,711
(Lee Chan) They're still
finalizing everything.

399
00:19:03,706 --> 00:19:06,170
Still, I wanted you to be
the first one to know.

400
00:19:06,237 --> 00:19:07,943
It's all thanks to your support.

401
00:19:08,010 --> 00:19:09,027
Thank you, Dareum.

402
00:19:09,094 --> 00:19:10,105
[Dareum reacts]

403
00:19:10,758 --> 00:19:12,256
I'm so happy for you, Chan.

404
00:19:12,323 --> 00:19:13,491
[Dareum laughs]

405
00:19:13,558 --> 00:19:14,572
[Dareum reacts]

406
00:19:15,327 --> 00:19:16,492
[glasses clink]

407
00:19:19,631 --> 00:19:20,562
[exhales]

408
00:19:20,629 --> 00:19:21,639
But...

409
00:19:22,668 --> 00:19:25,505
are you filming in the States?

410
00:19:26,209 --> 00:19:27,204
(Lee Chan) Yeah.

411
00:19:27,872 --> 00:19:28,839
[Lee Chan inhales]

412
00:19:28,906 --> 00:19:30,471
We'll start filming in LA

413
00:19:30,538 --> 00:19:31,939
early next year.

414
00:19:32,576 --> 00:19:33,545
[Dareum reacts]

415
00:19:33,612 --> 00:19:35,138
(Lee Chan) But the schedule
isn't confirmed yet.

416
00:19:36,772 --> 00:19:37,748
Then...

417
00:19:38,784 --> 00:19:40,684
I won't be able to see you for a while.

418
00:19:51,276 --> 00:19:52,496
Why don't you come with me?

419
00:19:54,658 --> 00:19:55,633
(Dareum) What?

420
00:19:56,330 --> 00:19:58,805
(Lee Chan) They're going to prepare
a car and housing in LA.

421
00:19:58,872 --> 00:20:00,805
[calm music]
While I'm filming,

422
00:20:00,872 --> 00:20:02,507
you can study fashion there.

423
00:20:02,574 --> 00:20:03,772
Then we can keep seeing each other.

424
00:20:04,208 --> 00:20:05,309
[Dareum grunts]

425
00:20:06,445 --> 00:20:07,778
What about work?

426
00:20:08,634 --> 00:20:10,332
We can work that out.

427
00:20:11,049 --> 00:20:12,816
Lots of people work remotely these days.

428
00:20:12,883 --> 00:20:15,772
(Lee Chan) Gaining experience there
might be better for you.

429
00:20:16,254 --> 00:20:17,285
[Dareum reacts]

430
00:20:18,516 --> 00:20:19,810
I'm sure you'll love it there.

431
00:20:20,271 --> 00:20:22,327
There are a lot of shows there,

432
00:20:22,394 --> 00:20:23,694
and lots of brands.

433
00:20:25,839 --> 00:20:26,931
[laughs awkwardly]

434
00:20:29,209 --> 00:20:30,162
I guess...

435
00:20:30,501 --> 00:20:31,370
that's true.

436
00:20:32,237 --> 00:20:33,337
(Lee Chan) That's why

437
00:20:33,939 --> 00:20:35,339
I picked one out for you too.

438
00:20:40,344 --> 00:20:41,387
[Dareum grunts]

439
00:20:42,762 --> 00:20:45,783
I have something to give you too.

440
00:20:46,684 --> 00:20:47,651
(Lee Chan) What is it?

441
00:20:51,105 --> 00:20:52,890
[rustles]

442
00:20:56,194 --> 00:20:57,328
[Dareum grunts]

443
00:20:59,431 --> 00:21:00,939
[rattles]

444
00:21:05,866 --> 00:21:06,973
(Lee Chan) A cardholder.

445
00:21:07,940 --> 00:21:11,739
(Dareum) Yes. I made it myself
at a leather workshop.

446
00:21:12,258 --> 00:21:13,737
(Lee Chan) You did a good job.

447
00:21:14,112 --> 00:21:15,579
It'll be too precious to use.

448
00:21:16,048 --> 00:21:17,114
[laughs awkwardly]

449
00:21:18,228 --> 00:21:19,250
Thank you.

450
00:21:28,811 --> 00:21:29,939
[sighs]

451
00:21:34,272 --> 00:21:35,699
[music stops]

452
00:21:41,974 --> 00:21:43,073
LA...

453
00:21:52,517 --> 00:21:54,196
[calm music]

454
00:21:55,165 --> 00:21:56,639
(Hagi) Whatever you decide,
[whoosh sound]

455
00:21:56,706 --> 00:21:59,890
just think about whether it's a choice
true to you.

456
00:21:59,957 --> 00:22:01,168
[whoosh sound]

457
00:22:15,774 --> 00:22:16,839
[sighs]

458
00:22:18,905 --> 00:22:20,705
(APPELLO
Outstanding employee)

459
00:22:21,345 --> 00:22:22,413
[faint sigh]

460
00:22:37,605 --> 00:22:39,605
(Proposal for APPELLO Brand Expansion
Marketing Team Nam Dareum)

461
00:22:40,829 --> 00:22:42,829
(APPELLO
Nam Dareum)

462
00:22:47,105 --> 00:22:48,205
[rattles]

463
00:22:49,141 --> 00:22:50,274
[Dareum sighs]

464
00:22:55,646 --> 00:22:56,848
[pen clicks]

465
00:22:56,915 --> 00:22:58,339
[writing sound]

466
00:23:04,625 --> 00:23:05,995
[music fades]

467
00:23:08,125 --> 00:23:09,693
[insects chirping]
(Mimi) Exhale as you go up.

468
00:23:09,760 --> 00:23:11,361
[Minwoo grunts]
[majestic music]

469
00:23:11,428 --> 00:23:13,164
And inhale as you go down.
[exhales]

470
00:23:13,231 --> 00:23:15,150
[inhales]

471
00:23:15,217 --> 00:23:17,405
Come up a little bit more.
[Minwoo grunts]

472
00:23:17,472 --> 00:23:19,344
[Minwoo groans]
[comical sound]

473
00:23:19,411 --> 00:23:21,405
And pause here. One, two.
[Minwoo grunts]

474
00:23:21,472 --> 00:23:22,706
[Minwoo exclaims]
[creaking sound]

475
00:23:22,773 --> 00:23:24,141
All right!
[Minwoo exhales]

476
00:23:24,208 --> 00:23:26,628
That's it for today.
[Minwoo sighs]

477
00:23:26,695 --> 00:23:27,544
[rustles]

478
00:23:27,611 --> 00:23:28,912
Please clean up your space.

479
00:23:29,514 --> 00:23:30,705
(Minwoo) Okay.
[grunts]

480
00:23:30,772 --> 00:23:31,972
[Minwoo exhales]
[music fades]

481
00:23:32,039 --> 00:23:34,772
- (Mimi) Good work today.
- (Minwoo) Thank you.

482
00:23:36,539 --> 00:23:37,956
[Minwoo grunts and pants]

483
00:23:38,023 --> 00:23:39,138
I...

484
00:23:40,263 --> 00:23:42,793
[Minwoo grunts]
[cheerful music]

485
00:23:42,860 --> 00:23:43,827
(Mimi) Minwoo!
[whoosh sound]

486
00:23:43,894 --> 00:23:46,024
You'll attend
the last session next time, right?

487
00:23:46,091 --> 00:23:48,068
[bubble popping sounds]
[grunts]

488
00:23:50,102 --> 00:23:52,922
I'm sure she was giving me a sign.

489
00:23:54,304 --> 00:23:55,228
[music stops]

490
00:23:55,295 --> 00:23:56,541
Was I mistaken?

491
00:23:56,608 --> 00:23:57,672
[wiping]

492
00:23:57,739 --> 00:23:58,842
[door closes]

493
00:24:07,785 --> 00:24:08,919
(Minwoo) I...

494
00:24:08,986 --> 00:24:11,555
Thank you for today.

495
00:24:11,622 --> 00:24:13,538
You too.

496
00:24:13,605 --> 00:24:14,758
(Minwoo) Right.
[bright music]

497
00:24:14,825 --> 00:24:17,272
I'll get going now, then.

498
00:24:17,839 --> 00:24:19,163
Bye!

499
00:24:21,565 --> 00:24:23,109
- (Mimi) Minwoo.
- (Minwoo) Yes?
[whoosh sound]

500
00:24:23,176 --> 00:24:24,572
Aren't we going together?
[whoosh sound]

501
00:24:24,639 --> 00:24:25,500
Right?

502
00:24:25,567 --> 00:24:28,138
(Minwoo) We're having
a meal together, right?

503
00:24:28,205 --> 00:24:29,806
- Let's go.
- Let's go!

504
00:24:30,902 --> 00:24:33,548
[Minwoo laughs]
[music stops]

505
00:24:33,615 --> 00:24:36,176
(Minwoo) This looks delicious.
[upbeat music plays]

506
00:24:36,243 --> 00:24:37,307
You must be hungry.

507
00:24:37,374 --> 00:24:39,116
(Mimi) Thank you.
[clatters]

508
00:24:39,183 --> 00:24:40,376
It was pretty tough today, right?

509
00:24:40,443 --> 00:24:42,472
(Minwoo) No, not at all.
I can handle that much.

510
00:24:43,347 --> 00:24:44,521
Thank you.

511
00:24:46,468 --> 00:24:48,258
(Mimi) You must be pretty outgoing,

512
00:24:48,759 --> 00:24:50,627
hitting on people at places like this.
[ding sound]

513
00:24:50,694 --> 00:24:51,922
(Minwoo) How did you get here?
[whoosh sound]

514
00:24:51,989 --> 00:24:52,829
(Mimi) By bus.
[cheerful music]

515
00:24:52,896 --> 00:24:55,634
(Minwoo) Then you can
go on a date with me on the way back.

516
00:24:55,701 --> 00:24:58,268
[shattering sound]
(Minwoo) Oh, you remember that?

517
00:24:59,438 --> 00:25:00,591
[groans]

518
00:25:01,340 --> 00:25:02,739
It was my first time!

519
00:25:02,806 --> 00:25:04,505
I mean it.

520
00:25:04,572 --> 00:25:07,846
I'm actually an introvert,
and I've never dated before.

521
00:25:07,913 --> 00:25:09,980
That day...

522
00:25:10,714 --> 00:25:13,685
I fell for you at first sight
and mustered up my courage.

523
00:25:13,752 --> 00:25:14,751
[faint laugh]

524
00:25:15,786 --> 00:25:18,241
That's what you say to every girl, right?

525
00:25:18,308 --> 00:25:19,581
(Minwoo) Yes.

526
00:25:19,648 --> 00:25:21,091
I'm just kidding.

527
00:25:21,158 --> 00:25:23,360
I usually...
[music stops]

528
00:25:23,427 --> 00:25:25,770
get a bit talkative
when I'm with someone I like.

529
00:25:25,837 --> 00:25:26,631
Why?

530
00:25:26,698 --> 00:25:28,439
Because I'm trying to pretend
that I'm not nervous.

531
00:25:30,520 --> 00:25:31,903
Then...

532
00:25:31,970 --> 00:25:32,967
what about now?

533
00:25:33,034 --> 00:25:34,238
I'm in this state right now.

534
00:25:35,261 --> 00:25:37,908
[trembling sound]
[whoosh sound]

535
00:25:37,975 --> 00:25:39,176
[comical sound]
[laughs]

536
00:25:39,243 --> 00:25:40,544
[bright music]
[laughs]

537
00:25:40,611 --> 00:25:42,638
That was funny, right? It worked.

538
00:25:42,705 --> 00:25:44,028
[Mimi clears throat]

539
00:25:44,095 --> 00:25:45,205
(Mimi) Anyway,

540
00:25:45,272 --> 00:25:47,818
thank you for dealing
with that customer last time.

541
00:25:47,885 --> 00:25:49,272
(Minwoo) Don't mention it.

542
00:25:49,906 --> 00:25:51,188
But...

543
00:25:51,255 --> 00:25:53,272
(Mimi) how do you know
all the terms and conditions?

544
00:25:53,339 --> 00:25:54,872
Nobody reads that.

545
00:25:56,198 --> 00:25:57,495
It's a habit.

546
00:25:57,562 --> 00:26:00,472
(Minwoo) A habit of thinking about winning
whenever I get in an argument.

547
00:26:01,138 --> 00:26:02,065
A habit?

548
00:26:02,472 --> 00:26:04,006
(Minwoo) Well...
[laughs awkwardly]

549
00:26:04,073 --> 00:26:05,665
Reading is part of my job.

550
00:26:05,732 --> 00:26:06,543
[faint laugh]

551
00:26:06,610 --> 00:26:07,767
[glasses clink]

552
00:26:09,238 --> 00:26:10,854
(Mimi) Who is this guy?

553
00:26:10,921 --> 00:26:12,342
There's an unexpected charm to him.

554
00:26:15,728 --> 00:26:16,836
[faint laugh]
[glass clunks]

555
00:26:16,903 --> 00:26:17,948
[music stops]

556
00:26:19,058 --> 00:26:20,492
[elegant music plays]

557
00:26:21,353 --> 00:26:22,439
[Lee Chan laughs]

558
00:26:23,757 --> 00:26:25,104
(Lee Chan) You gave it an update.

559
00:26:25,171 --> 00:26:27,814
Wow, there's an LA version now.

560
00:26:27,881 --> 00:26:29,006
[rustling]

561
00:26:29,560 --> 00:26:31,286
(Dareum) You've always said

562
00:26:31,353 --> 00:26:32,997
that going to Hollywood was your dream.

563
00:26:33,064 --> 00:26:34,432
(Lee Chan) Yeah.

564
00:26:34,499 --> 00:26:36,606
So I've imagined it loads of times too.

565
00:26:37,700 --> 00:26:38,706
(Lee Chan) Then...

566
00:26:39,304 --> 00:26:40,671
we can do all of these together.

567
00:26:41,940 --> 00:26:42,973
[laughs]

568
00:26:44,706 --> 00:26:47,039
Seeing the stars at the observatory,

569
00:26:47,878 --> 00:26:49,346
walking on the beach together...

570
00:26:50,480 --> 00:26:51,968
It's a perfect date plan.

571
00:26:52,035 --> 00:26:53,016
[laughs]

572
00:26:54,119 --> 00:26:55,138
[laughs]

573
00:27:01,365 --> 00:27:02,305
(Dareum) Chan.

574
00:27:03,180 --> 00:27:04,528
I have something to tell you.

575
00:27:06,606 --> 00:27:07,431
Something to tell me?

576
00:27:07,917 --> 00:27:09,066
[inhales]

577
00:27:09,698 --> 00:27:10,701
(Dareum) I...

578
00:27:11,947 --> 00:27:13,303
liked spending time

579
00:27:14,954 --> 00:27:15,939
with you.

580
00:27:16,458 --> 00:27:17,708
I felt excited too.

581
00:27:20,791 --> 00:27:21,778
But...

582
00:27:24,121 --> 00:27:25,282
I couldn't...

583
00:27:26,508 --> 00:27:27,751
be honest.

584
00:27:32,257 --> 00:27:33,272
What do you mean?

585
00:27:34,226 --> 00:27:35,259
I couldn't be honest with you

586
00:27:36,382 --> 00:27:37,327
or...

587
00:27:38,962 --> 00:27:40,297
with myself.

588
00:27:42,459 --> 00:27:43,533
(Dareum) So today,

589
00:27:44,334 --> 00:27:45,769
I'll stop pretending to be okay

590
00:27:46,970 --> 00:27:48,505
and be honest with you.

591
00:27:50,742 --> 00:27:51,942
[inhales]

592
00:27:52,405 --> 00:27:53,844
[laughs]

593
00:27:55,647 --> 00:27:57,019
[grunts]

594
00:27:59,388 --> 00:28:01,500
I thought that
when I was with someone I liked,

595
00:28:02,283 --> 00:28:03,520
I'd be able

596
00:28:04,456 --> 00:28:05,522
to laugh,

597
00:28:06,091 --> 00:28:09,159
cry, whine, express anger,

598
00:28:10,776 --> 00:28:13,063
and share all my emotions with them.

599
00:28:14,915 --> 00:28:15,932
But...

600
00:28:17,013 --> 00:28:18,106
I...

601
00:28:22,279 --> 00:28:23,407
couldn't really

602
00:28:25,053 --> 00:28:26,677
do that with you.

603
00:28:28,638 --> 00:28:30,420
[calm music]

604
00:28:32,332 --> 00:28:33,650
I think

605
00:28:34,727 --> 00:28:35,952
I still consider you

606
00:28:36,688 --> 00:28:37,654
as someone

607
00:28:38,557 --> 00:28:39,656
I admire

608
00:28:40,843 --> 00:28:42,259
rather than a romantic partner.

609
00:28:46,574 --> 00:28:48,598
Of course, I still support your dream,

610
00:28:49,790 --> 00:28:51,505
but I have my own dream too now.

611
00:28:52,616 --> 00:28:55,038
Going to the States would be great,

612
00:28:55,946 --> 00:28:57,074
but I love APPELLO,

613
00:29:00,209 --> 00:29:01,472
and I love the work

614
00:29:02,546 --> 00:29:03,580
I'm doing here more.

615
00:29:05,306 --> 00:29:06,350
So...

616
00:29:07,662 --> 00:29:09,653
I want to remain an employee of APPELLO

617
00:29:14,172 --> 00:29:15,392
and as...

618
00:29:19,870 --> 00:29:20,997
your fan.

619
00:29:29,675 --> 00:29:31,105
[Dareum exhales]

620
00:29:39,227 --> 00:29:40,664
[music stops]

621
00:29:42,187 --> 00:29:43,692
[street sounds]

622
00:29:56,905 --> 00:29:59,004
[Yeongwoo scoffs]
Nam Dareum mode has started again.

623
00:29:59,071 --> 00:30:01,471
"Nam Dareum mode"? What's that?

624
00:30:01,538 --> 00:30:03,540
(Yeongwoo) Remember last time
when we made the challenge video?

625
00:30:03,607 --> 00:30:05,809
She worked even harder when
we were told to stop working on it.
[Mina reacts]

626
00:30:05,876 --> 00:30:09,054
Nam Dareum mode turns on
when she's at the edge of a cliff!

627
00:30:09,121 --> 00:30:12,382
Ms. Nam, you're not standing
at the edge of a cliff, are you?

628
00:30:12,449 --> 00:30:14,153
Is something going on?

629
00:30:14,220 --> 00:30:16,339
No, it's nothing...

630
00:30:17,161 --> 00:30:19,483
I just like that I can take
my mind off things.
[laughs awkwardly]

631
00:30:19,550 --> 00:30:21,536
[rattling]

632
00:30:23,493 --> 00:30:25,610
(Mina) Ms. Nam,
what happened to your hand?

633
00:30:25,634 --> 00:30:26,538
Did you hurt yourself?

634
00:30:26,605 --> 00:30:27,632
(Dareum) Oh, this?

635
00:30:27,699 --> 00:30:30,368
I'm fostering a kitten right now.
[Mina, Yeongwoo gasps]

636
00:30:30,435 --> 00:30:32,841
I need to find a home for the kitten,

637
00:30:32,908 --> 00:30:34,672
but I've been too busy these days.

638
00:30:34,739 --> 00:30:35,738
(Yeongwoo) A kitten?

639
00:30:35,805 --> 00:30:37,790
I was actually preparing to adopt one.

640
00:30:37,857 --> 00:30:39,619
Hang on... Can I see a photo?

641
00:30:39,686 --> 00:30:40,797
- Really?
- (Yeongwoo) Yeah!

642
00:30:40,864 --> 00:30:41,906
Hang on.

643
00:30:42,512 --> 00:30:44,918
Mr. Park, you like animals?

644
00:30:44,985 --> 00:30:46,149
Yes, I love them.

645
00:30:46,216 --> 00:30:48,639
Me too.
[Dareum inhales]

646
00:30:48,706 --> 00:30:50,329
(Dareum) Isn't it cute?
[cat meowing sound]
[cheerful music]

647
00:30:50,396 --> 00:30:51,721
[Mina, Yeongwoo gasp]

648
00:30:51,788 --> 00:30:53,032
Its name is Jjak.

649
00:30:53,099 --> 00:30:54,268
I actually found two of them together.

650
00:30:54,335 --> 00:30:56,533
They're Koong and Jjak.

651
00:30:56,600 --> 00:30:59,171
Oh, gosh. It's so cute!

652
00:30:59,238 --> 00:31:01,674
I swear, I really wanted
to adopt an orange cat.

653
00:31:01,741 --> 00:31:03,272
- For real?
- (Yeongwoo) For real.

654
00:31:03,902 --> 00:31:06,102
Here's another photo.
[Yeongwoo, Mina gasp]

655
00:31:06,169 --> 00:31:07,971
(Mina) It's so cute!
[Yeongwoo reacts]

656
00:31:08,038 --> 00:31:09,507
(Mina) So cute.
[music stops]

657
00:31:09,574 --> 00:31:10,707
[door opens]

658
00:31:11,777 --> 00:31:13,207
[door closes]
[footsteps approaching]

659
00:31:13,274 --> 00:31:14,544
[Wonbin exhales]

660
00:31:18,190 --> 00:31:19,831
(Wonbin) Director Park Chandong's script.

661
00:31:19,898 --> 00:31:20,817
Chan!

662
00:31:21,451 --> 00:31:23,038
You've officially been cast!

663
00:31:23,105 --> 00:31:24,089
[claps]
Yeah!

664
00:31:24,156 --> 00:31:25,906
[Wonbin exclaims]

665
00:31:26,858 --> 00:31:28,105
Wow...

666
00:31:29,795 --> 00:31:31,805
What is it? Is it hard to believe?

667
00:31:31,872 --> 00:31:32,731
(Lee Chan) What?

668
00:31:32,798 --> 00:31:34,138
No, I'm just really happy.

669
00:31:34,205 --> 00:31:35,101
[scoffs]

670
00:31:35,634 --> 00:31:37,066
Is that the problem?

671
00:31:37,133 --> 00:31:39,454
(Wonbin) All right.
Let's save the celebration for later.

672
00:31:39,521 --> 00:31:41,471
There's a lot to prepare for
since it's shot in the States.

673
00:31:41,538 --> 00:31:44,880
We have to adjust your schedule,
get a visa, get in shape...

674
00:31:44,947 --> 00:31:46,878
And if there's anything you need,
write up a list...

675
00:31:46,945 --> 00:31:49,105
I don't think I can just leave like this.
[taps]

676
00:31:50,616 --> 00:31:52,315
(Wonbin) Chan! Where are you going?

677
00:32:07,299 --> 00:32:08,398
[door closes]

678
00:32:09,368 --> 00:32:10,433
[knocks]

679
00:32:11,368 --> 00:32:12,456
[Dareum reacts]

680
00:32:12,523 --> 00:32:13,637
Mr. Kang.

681
00:32:17,073 --> 00:32:18,252
You haven't gone home yet?

682
00:32:18,319 --> 00:32:19,105
(Dareum) Oh...
[laughs awkwardly]

683
00:32:19,172 --> 00:32:20,973
I want to get some more done
before I leave.

684
00:32:26,439 --> 00:32:27,439
[thuds]

685
00:32:28,487 --> 00:32:29,953
[bright music]

686
00:32:31,790 --> 00:32:34,572
It's fine...
[Hagi sighs]

687
00:32:37,396 --> 00:32:38,595
Thank you.

688
00:32:43,842 --> 00:32:44,801
(Hagi) Do you

689
00:32:45,304 --> 00:32:46,469
not have a date today?

690
00:32:47,139 --> 00:32:48,105
(Dareum) No.

691
00:32:48,172 --> 00:32:52,277
[inhales]
There's so much work,
I don't have time for a date.

692
00:32:52,344 --> 00:32:53,912
Why are you doing everything on your own?

693
00:32:53,979 --> 00:32:55,378
(Hagi) I didn't tell you to do that.

694
00:32:55,445 --> 00:32:56,996
[laughs awkwardly]

695
00:32:57,063 --> 00:32:58,917
My colleagues helped me out earlier.

696
00:32:58,984 --> 00:33:00,039
(Dareum) But...

697
00:33:00,753 --> 00:33:02,052
I just wanted to finish up by myself.

698
00:33:02,635 --> 00:33:04,073
It must be tough suddenly being in charge

699
00:33:05,102 --> 00:33:06,189
of a large event.

700
00:33:06,699 --> 00:33:08,138
[inhales]
[laughs awkwardly]

701
00:33:08,205 --> 00:33:10,869
I do feel a bit overwhelmed,

702
00:33:11,339 --> 00:33:12,262
but still...

703
00:33:12,722 --> 00:33:15,332
(Dareum) I feel proud
being in charge of a project.

704
00:33:26,659 --> 00:33:28,138
(Hagi) I'm sure you'll learn
a lot of things

705
00:33:29,472 --> 00:33:30,814
during the process.

706
00:33:31,810 --> 00:33:33,054
(Dareum) Right.

707
00:33:33,121 --> 00:33:34,788
[gasps]
Right.

708
00:33:34,855 --> 00:33:38,039
Mr. Park said he wants
to adopt Koong and Jjak.

709
00:33:38,457 --> 00:33:39,456
What?

710
00:33:39,956 --> 00:33:41,576
You're sending them away already?

711
00:33:41,643 --> 00:33:44,073
I do feel sad about sending them away,

712
00:33:44,140 --> 00:33:46,606
but this is a great opportunity
for Koong and Jjak.

713
00:33:47,548 --> 00:33:48,372
Well, that's true.

714
00:33:48,439 --> 00:33:49,566
(Dareum) Yeah.
[laughs]

715
00:33:49,633 --> 00:33:53,138
I bought a lot of toys for Koong, though.

716
00:33:53,205 --> 00:33:55,055
What else did you buy this time?

717
00:33:55,122 --> 00:33:57,001
(Dareum) I told you
that you didn't need to buy more.

718
00:33:58,192 --> 00:33:59,238
[claps]

719
00:34:00,345 --> 00:34:01,544
Where did you buy them?

720
00:34:02,214 --> 00:34:04,270
(Hagi) Just somewhere...
[music stops]

721
00:34:04,337 --> 00:34:05,916
[Dareum laughs]
[elevator doors opening]

722
00:34:10,980 --> 00:34:12,290
(Miyeong) Ms. Nam?

723
00:34:12,357 --> 00:34:14,706
She said she'll be working late today.
[elevator doors closing]

724
00:34:16,262 --> 00:34:17,187
[card reader beeps]

725
00:34:27,339 --> 00:34:29,872
[door closes]
[sad music]

726
00:35:00,943 --> 00:35:02,357
[music stops]

727
00:35:09,154 --> 00:35:10,073
[faint laugh]

728
00:35:10,689 --> 00:35:11,681
Mr. Kang.

729
00:35:12,228 --> 00:35:14,884
(Dareum) Do you remember
what you told me last time?

730
00:35:16,583 --> 00:35:18,584
(Hagi) What do you mean?
[rustles]

731
00:35:19,241 --> 00:35:22,806
You told me to think about whether
the choice I make is true to myself.

732
00:35:25,323 --> 00:35:26,872
[Hagi laughs]
[Dareum laughs awkwardly]

733
00:35:29,117 --> 00:35:30,439
(Dareum) Thanks to what you said...

734
00:35:31,436 --> 00:35:32,702
I mustered up my courage.

735
00:35:36,942 --> 00:35:38,555
[calm music]

736
00:35:40,030 --> 00:35:41,077
[grunts]

737
00:35:42,195 --> 00:35:43,279
For the first time,

738
00:35:45,081 --> 00:35:46,416
I was really honest.

739
00:35:48,053 --> 00:35:49,853
And I made a choice true to myself.

740
00:35:53,463 --> 00:35:55,125
[laughs]
Thank you, Mr. Kang.

741
00:36:00,463 --> 00:36:02,939
You were just always someone
who could make

742
00:36:04,810 --> 00:36:06,073
that choice.

743
00:36:09,050 --> 00:36:10,373
[laughs awkwardly]

744
00:36:12,780 --> 00:36:14,705
Hearing you say it like that,

745
00:36:14,772 --> 00:36:16,073
I guess it's true.

746
00:36:18,283 --> 00:36:19,449
[Dareum laughs awkwardly]

747
00:36:21,119 --> 00:36:22,985
(Hagi) So she ended things...
[rattles]

748
00:36:23,052 --> 00:36:24,073
with that man.

749
00:36:35,286 --> 00:36:36,238
Ms. Nam.

750
00:36:36,703 --> 00:36:37,634
(Dareum) Yes?

751
00:36:39,768 --> 00:36:41,473
I have something to say...
[door opens]

752
00:36:41,540 --> 00:36:43,575
(Lee Chan) You're working late.
[music stops]

753
00:36:43,642 --> 00:36:44,570
[door closes]

754
00:36:45,509 --> 00:36:46,639
(Hagi) What brings you here?

755
00:36:47,142 --> 00:36:49,412
(Lee Chan) I heard you were working late
because of the pop-up event.

756
00:36:50,182 --> 00:36:52,405
So these are the DIY kits?

757
00:36:53,018 --> 00:36:54,639
Yes, Director.

758
00:36:55,885 --> 00:36:57,687
[quiet music]

759
00:37:01,212 --> 00:37:02,379
How do I do this?

760
00:37:02,446 --> 00:37:03,539
(Lee Chan) Teach me.

761
00:37:05,171 --> 00:37:06,596
(Hagi) Sit down.

762
00:37:09,234 --> 00:37:10,877
[chair rattles]

763
00:37:15,574 --> 00:37:17,355
[playful music]

764
00:37:21,806 --> 00:37:24,814
You're really fast, Director.

765
00:37:24,881 --> 00:37:28,181
(Lee Chan) I've signed over
a thousand albums in one day, you know.

766
00:37:28,248 --> 00:37:29,485
This is nothing.

767
00:37:29,888 --> 00:37:31,221
Fold them properly.

768
00:37:31,721 --> 00:37:33,537
Don't just rush through them.
Pay attention to the details.

769
00:37:33,604 --> 00:37:34,639
[laughs]

770
00:37:34,706 --> 00:37:36,059
Yes, Mr. Kang.

771
00:37:41,266 --> 00:37:42,606
Ms. Nam, here.

772
00:37:43,384 --> 00:37:44,973
(Dareum) Oh...
[thuds]

773
00:37:47,182 --> 00:37:48,579
[music stops]

774
00:37:50,309 --> 00:37:52,839
(Lee Chan) But Ms. Nam,

775
00:37:53,312 --> 00:37:54,644
who are you more compatible with?

776
00:37:55,278 --> 00:37:56,376
Him or me?

777
00:37:56,443 --> 00:37:58,114
[intriguing music]

778
00:37:58,181 --> 00:37:59,148
(Dareum) Excuse me?

779
00:37:59,952 --> 00:38:01,251
Why are you asking that?

780
00:38:02,621 --> 00:38:04,387
You know, people have preferences.

781
00:38:07,248 --> 00:38:08,205
[Dareum grunts]

782
00:38:09,624 --> 00:38:11,372
[Dareum stammers]
I...

783
00:38:11,439 --> 00:38:13,696
[laughs awkwardly]
Well...

784
00:38:13,763 --> 00:38:14,799
[Dareum stammers]

785
00:38:14,866 --> 00:38:16,032
I...
[laughs awkwardly]

786
00:38:16,099 --> 00:38:18,606
I'm still a new employee...

787
00:38:19,137 --> 00:38:22,872
And you have
different personalities, so...

788
00:38:26,335 --> 00:38:29,505
That's a safe, diplomatic answer.
[music stops]

789
00:38:34,507 --> 00:38:35,518
(Lee Chan) I was just...

790
00:38:36,171 --> 00:38:38,087
wondering if you're more drawn
to one of us.

791
00:38:40,479 --> 00:38:42,141
[calm music]

792
00:38:50,102 --> 00:38:51,333
[faint sigh]

793
00:38:53,625 --> 00:38:55,322
[rattling]

794
00:39:01,501 --> 00:39:02,777
[music stops]

795
00:39:08,931 --> 00:39:10,372
[rattling]

796
00:39:18,118 --> 00:39:19,270
[thuds]

797
00:39:25,057 --> 00:39:27,372
[grabs]
[somber music]

798
00:39:31,369 --> 00:39:33,004
Let me talk to you.
[music fades]

799
00:39:36,815 --> 00:39:37,847
(Hagi) Did you...

800
00:39:38,766 --> 00:39:40,216
really come here because of work?

801
00:39:41,274 --> 00:39:42,218
(Lee Chan) Why?

802
00:39:42,854 --> 00:39:44,454
(Hagi) And when you came
to Ms. Im Cheongrim's home too.

803
00:39:48,933 --> 00:39:50,493
This is an important project.

804
00:39:52,473 --> 00:39:53,529
Do you...

805
00:39:55,434 --> 00:39:56,532
like Ms. Nam, by any chance?

806
00:39:57,336 --> 00:39:58,968
[ominous music]

807
00:40:01,272 --> 00:40:02,472
[exhales]

808
00:40:04,352 --> 00:40:05,441
I do.

809
00:40:10,564 --> 00:40:11,848
She's my favorite employee.

810
00:40:13,552 --> 00:40:15,685
(Lee Chan) Who wouldn't like her
when she works so hard?

811
00:40:16,392 --> 00:40:17,453
Only as an employee?

812
00:40:18,946 --> 00:40:20,423
What is it you want to hear?

813
00:40:21,339 --> 00:40:23,359
You were going
to go after Ms. Nam just now too.

814
00:40:27,600 --> 00:40:28,698
What about you?

815
00:40:30,199 --> 00:40:31,901
(Lee Chan) Are you protecting an employee,

816
00:40:32,529 --> 00:40:33,770
or are you threatened by me?

817
00:40:40,204 --> 00:40:41,444
You're not telling me either.

818
00:40:45,915 --> 00:40:48,305
If you're honest with me,
[Lee Chan sighs]

819
00:40:51,376 --> 00:40:52,488
then I'll be honest too.

820
00:41:02,467 --> 00:41:04,167
[music fades]

821
00:41:12,896 --> 00:41:14,045
[sighs]

822
00:41:19,165 --> 00:41:20,272
(Lee Chan) Ms. Nam,

823
00:41:21,205 --> 00:41:23,553
who are you more compatible with?
Him or me?

824
00:41:24,913 --> 00:41:26,222
[calm music]

825
00:41:26,758 --> 00:41:28,038
I want
[birds singing]

826
00:41:28,105 --> 00:41:30,604
to date you, Dareum.

827
00:41:31,530 --> 00:41:33,801
I'm sorry about that day.

828
00:41:33,868 --> 00:41:36,534
(Dareum) It's fine.

829
00:41:36,601 --> 00:41:38,474
(Lee Chan) I feel bad
just letting you go like this.

830
00:41:38,541 --> 00:41:41,192
(Dareum) I'm really fine.
[Dareum laughs]

831
00:41:41,259 --> 00:41:42,438
(Hagi) You're not fine.

832
00:41:43,175 --> 00:41:44,240
At least to me,

833
00:41:44,810 --> 00:41:46,142
you can say that you're not fine.

834
00:41:48,405 --> 00:41:49,812
[writing]

835
00:41:51,286 --> 00:41:52,315
[faint sigh]

836
00:41:53,572 --> 00:41:54,584
(Lee Chan) I was just

837
00:41:54,984 --> 00:41:57,228
wondering if you're more drawn
to one of us.

838
00:41:57,295 --> 00:41:58,842
[inhales]
[music stops]

839
00:42:01,438 --> 00:42:03,359
[doorbell rings]
[insects chirping]

840
00:42:03,426 --> 00:42:05,261
(Seula) Just a moment!
[door lock sound]

841
00:42:05,328 --> 00:42:06,662
Thank you.
[rustles]

842
00:42:06,729 --> 00:42:08,412
(delivery man) Enjoy your food,
and have a great day.

843
00:42:08,479 --> 00:42:10,339
[thud sound]
[uplifting music]

844
00:42:11,349 --> 00:42:12,805
(Roy) Have a great day.

845
00:42:12,872 --> 00:42:14,003
[whoosh sound]

846
00:42:14,070 --> 00:42:16,441
I hope my voice brings happiness
[whoosh sound]

847
00:42:16,508 --> 00:42:18,505
to your everyday life.

848
00:42:19,011 --> 00:42:21,210
This was Roy of D.N.X.

849
00:42:24,126 --> 00:42:25,606
[thuds]
[music stops]

850
00:42:29,013 --> 00:42:30,443
[engine revs]

851
00:42:33,358 --> 00:42:35,138
[Seula pants]

852
00:42:36,172 --> 00:42:38,489
I'm sure that was Roy's voice.

853
00:42:38,556 --> 00:42:40,325
[pants]

854
00:42:44,073 --> 00:42:45,768
[door opens]

855
00:42:47,270 --> 00:42:49,105
[ominous music]

856
00:42:50,839 --> 00:42:52,074
[door opens]

857
00:42:56,939 --> 00:42:58,016
(Yeongwoo) No...
[Mina grunts]
[music stops]

858
00:42:58,083 --> 00:42:59,584
(Yeongwoo) I wanted
to have kalguksu today.

859
00:42:59,651 --> 00:43:01,484
[Mina groans]
(Dareum) We failed again.

860
00:43:01,551 --> 00:43:03,986
[Mina groans]
When will we ever
get to try the kalguksu?

861
00:43:04,053 --> 00:43:04,941
I don't think we'll have a chance

862
00:43:05,008 --> 00:43:07,639
unless we take the morning off
and wait in line for hours.

863
00:43:07,706 --> 00:43:10,559
I really wanted to try that place.
[Mina grunts]

864
00:43:10,626 --> 00:43:12,086
(Mina) Me too.

865
00:43:12,153 --> 00:43:14,920
Why don't we go up to the rooftop garden
and walk off our meal?

866
00:43:14,987 --> 00:43:15,998
- (Yeongwoo) Sounds great.
- (Mina) Right?

867
00:43:16,065 --> 00:43:18,304
I have work to do,
so I'll head inside first.
[Dareum laughs]

868
00:43:18,371 --> 00:43:20,572
Then should we go together?
[Dareum reacts]

869
00:43:20,639 --> 00:43:21,570
(Mina) Sure!

870
00:43:21,637 --> 00:43:22,440
- (Dareum) See you later.
- (Yeongwoo) Okay.

871
00:43:22,507 --> 00:43:24,672
[button clicks]
(Mina) See you later.

872
00:43:25,316 --> 00:43:26,442
[card reader beeps]

873
00:43:29,039 --> 00:43:29,945
[Dareum reacts]
[Hyesu grunts]

874
00:43:30,012 --> 00:43:31,747
Ms. Seo, didn't you have lunch?

875
00:43:31,814 --> 00:43:33,138
(Hyesu) I should eat now.

876
00:43:33,752 --> 00:43:35,126
I guess you had lunch early.

877
00:43:35,193 --> 00:43:37,305
- Yes. Enjoy your lunch.
- (Hyesu) Yeah.
[Dareum laughs]

878
00:43:40,826 --> 00:43:42,872
[door opens]
[ominous sound effect]

879
00:43:44,136 --> 00:43:45,815
[tense music]

880
00:43:57,405 --> 00:43:59,408
Did Ms. Cheon clean here?

881
00:44:04,918 --> 00:44:06,682
[ominous sound effect]

882
00:44:07,439 --> 00:44:09,172
[music fades]

883
00:44:10,448 --> 00:44:11,613
[Minwoo scoffs]

884
00:44:11,680 --> 00:44:14,000
People would think
you're moving away at this hour.

885
00:44:14,067 --> 00:44:15,961
Why do you have so much stuff
for just one cat?
[bell ringing]

886
00:44:16,028 --> 00:44:17,639
They just piled up.

887
00:44:22,085 --> 00:44:23,906
(Minwoo) Here.
[door closes]
[cat meowing]

888
00:44:23,973 --> 00:44:25,872
Hand the cat over safely,

889
00:44:26,772 --> 00:44:28,037
and tell her how you feel too.

890
00:44:28,104 --> 00:44:29,772
[bubble popping sound]
[cheerful music]

891
00:44:30,499 --> 00:44:31,605
What are you talking about?

892
00:44:31,672 --> 00:44:34,174
(Minwoo) Today's the perfect opportunity.
Don't miss it.
[cat meowing]

893
00:44:34,241 --> 00:44:35,311
Make sure to tell her!

894
00:44:35,378 --> 00:44:37,678
(Hagi) Jeez. Just go.

895
00:44:37,745 --> 00:44:38,839
[Hagi grunts]

896
00:44:40,085 --> 00:44:42,405
Good luck, okay?

897
00:44:43,739 --> 00:44:45,788
- (Hagi) Go.
- (Minwoo) I'm going.

898
00:44:50,808 --> 00:44:51,827
Tell her how I feel?

899
00:44:52,397 --> 00:44:54,505
[comical sound]
(Minwoo) Tell her how you feel too.

900
00:44:54,572 --> 00:44:55,624
[bubble popping sound]

901
00:44:55,691 --> 00:44:56,937
[inhales]
[comical sound]

902
00:44:57,004 --> 00:44:58,905
(Luni) Someone close.

903
00:44:58,972 --> 00:45:00,171
[bubble popping sound]

904
00:45:00,238 --> 00:45:01,603
[sighs]

905
00:45:11,291 --> 00:45:13,082
[music stops]
[clicks]

906
00:45:13,149 --> 00:45:14,511
[cat meowing]
[phone vibrating]

907
00:45:14,578 --> 00:45:16,112
[bells ringing]

908
00:45:16,179 --> 00:45:17,205
(Dareum) Hang on.

909
00:45:20,119 --> 00:45:21,672
[message notification sound]
(Hagi) Let's meet around eight.

910
00:45:21,739 --> 00:45:22,672
[Dareum reacts]

911
00:45:22,739 --> 00:45:26,447
[message notification sound]
(Dareum) Okay. Koong and Jjak
are finally meeting.

912
00:45:26,514 --> 00:45:29,441
(Hagi) There's a lot of luggage,
so I'll head over to your place.
[message notification sound]

913
00:45:29,508 --> 00:45:30,633
[message notification sound]
I'm heading out now.

914
00:45:31,100 --> 00:45:33,519
He really is considerate.

915
00:45:33,586 --> 00:45:35,133
[phone clacks]
[thuds]

916
00:45:37,626 --> 00:45:39,642
[gasps]
[dramatic music]

917
00:45:39,709 --> 00:45:41,510
[gasps]
[whoosh sound]

918
00:45:41,577 --> 00:45:42,972
[gasps]
[whoosh sound]

919
00:45:43,039 --> 00:45:44,305
[sparkling sound]
(Lee Chan) See you, Dareum!

920
00:45:44,372 --> 00:45:46,215
[gasps]
[thud sound]

921
00:45:46,282 --> 00:45:47,877
[whoosh sound]
[gasps]

922
00:45:49,087 --> 00:45:51,038
If Mr. Kang sees this...
[music stops]

923
00:45:51,105 --> 00:45:52,138
No!

924
00:45:52,205 --> 00:45:53,748
[exciting music]

925
00:45:53,815 --> 00:45:55,914
[thud sound]
[Dareum yelps]

926
00:45:56,278 --> 00:45:57,806
Darn it...

927
00:45:58,382 --> 00:45:59,584
[grunts]

928
00:46:00,499 --> 00:46:01,707
[Dareum grunts]

929
00:46:04,119 --> 00:46:05,401
[clatters]

930
00:46:08,907 --> 00:46:11,006
All right...
[pants]

931
00:46:12,339 --> 00:46:13,745
[whoosh sound]
[music stops]

932
00:46:13,812 --> 00:46:15,006
[groans]

933
00:46:16,277 --> 00:46:17,382
[brushes hands]

934
00:46:17,449 --> 00:46:19,930
[thuds]

935
00:46:20,719 --> 00:46:21,817
[brushes hands]

936
00:46:28,354 --> 00:46:29,425
[sighs]
[comical sound]

937
00:46:29,492 --> 00:46:30,729
(Minwoo) Tell her how you feel too.

938
00:46:30,796 --> 00:46:31,856
[bubble popping sound]

939
00:46:34,939 --> 00:46:35,939
[Dareum gasps]

940
00:46:36,006 --> 00:46:37,986
(Dareum) Hi, Koong.

941
00:46:38,053 --> 00:46:39,104
[cat meowing]

942
00:46:39,171 --> 00:46:41,136
[exclaims]
[Hagi brushes hands]

943
00:46:41,973 --> 00:46:43,672
Hang on.
[cat meowing]

944
00:46:44,299 --> 00:46:46,596
It must have been heavy.
Thank you, Mr. Kang.

945
00:46:46,663 --> 00:46:47,739
(Hagi) It's nothing.

946
00:46:48,947 --> 00:46:49,912
(Dareum) Right!

947
00:46:51,617 --> 00:46:52,615
Wear these.

948
00:46:54,547 --> 00:46:56,006
Well, I...

949
00:46:56,734 --> 00:46:57,653
(Dareum) Yes?

950
00:46:59,108 --> 00:47:01,857
It's my first time at a woman's place...

951
00:47:02,491 --> 00:47:03,338
[cheerful music]
(Dareum) I see...

952
00:47:03,405 --> 00:47:05,638
(Hagi) Please excuse me.

953
00:47:05,705 --> 00:47:07,072
[laughs awkwardly]
Right.

954
00:47:07,139 --> 00:47:08,238
Make yourself at home.

955
00:47:11,133 --> 00:47:12,163
[Dareum laughs awkwardly]

956
00:47:14,306 --> 00:47:15,805
[Dareum laughs]

957
00:47:16,875 --> 00:47:18,440
Take your time.

958
00:47:18,507 --> 00:47:20,276
[music stops]
[boiling]

959
00:47:21,969 --> 00:47:22,911
[bubble popping sound]

960
00:47:22,978 --> 00:47:23,912
[whoosh sound]

961
00:47:23,979 --> 00:47:26,017
[intriguing music]
[cup clinks]

962
00:47:26,084 --> 00:47:27,467
[door closes]

963
00:47:27,534 --> 00:47:29,221
[Hagi clears throat]
[Dareum grunts]

964
00:47:29,288 --> 00:47:30,472
[rattles]

965
00:47:31,023 --> 00:47:33,155
[cup thuds]
[pouring]

966
00:47:36,125 --> 00:47:37,486
Here, have some tea.

967
00:47:37,553 --> 00:47:39,539
Thank you.

968
00:47:47,052 --> 00:47:48,810
[laughs awkwardly]
[cat meowing]

969
00:47:48,877 --> 00:47:50,319
[music fades]

970
00:47:51,076 --> 00:47:53,542
(Dareum) Jjak.

971
00:47:54,472 --> 00:47:55,596
[Dareum grunts]

972
00:47:55,663 --> 00:47:58,680
Koong is here.

973
00:47:58,747 --> 00:48:00,682
Jjak has grown a lot.

974
00:48:00,749 --> 00:48:01,955
Really?

975
00:48:02,022 --> 00:48:03,485
Isn't Koong a similar size?

976
00:48:03,552 --> 00:48:04,987
Well, Koong...

977
00:48:06,455 --> 00:48:07,723
[grunts]

978
00:48:07,790 --> 00:48:09,058
Where did Koong go?

979
00:48:09,125 --> 00:48:10,829
[Dareum grunts]

980
00:48:10,896 --> 00:48:12,006
Koong.
[cat meowing]

981
00:48:12,073 --> 00:48:13,808
[cheerful music]

982
00:48:16,001 --> 00:48:17,299
When did Koong go all the way over there?

983
00:48:19,359 --> 00:48:20,603
I'll get Koong.
[music stops]

984
00:48:21,776 --> 00:48:23,105
- Koong.
- (Dareum) What?

985
00:48:23,680 --> 00:48:24,740
(Hagi) Koong.

986
00:48:24,807 --> 00:48:25,877
[tense music]

987
00:48:25,944 --> 00:48:27,609
[panting]
(Dareum) Hang on, Jjak.

988
00:48:27,676 --> 00:48:28,672
No...

989
00:48:28,739 --> 00:48:30,779
Koong.
[whoosh sound]

990
00:48:33,572 --> 00:48:35,184
- (Dareum) Wait!
- (Hagi) Oh, gosh...
[music stops]

991
00:48:35,251 --> 00:48:38,038
You can't look in here!

992
00:48:38,105 --> 00:48:38,887
My secret...

993
00:48:38,954 --> 00:48:40,706
[intriguing music]
(Dareum) I mean...

994
00:48:41,286 --> 00:48:43,292
My underwear is in there...

995
00:48:43,662 --> 00:48:44,727
(Hagi) Oh...

996
00:48:45,394 --> 00:48:47,839
Sorry. Then...
[Dareum laughs awkwardly]

997
00:48:49,267 --> 00:48:51,238
I won't look.

998
00:48:51,305 --> 00:48:53,335
[Dareum sighs]

999
00:48:53,969 --> 00:48:55,772
[whoosh sound]
["peek-a-boo" sound]

1000
00:48:56,437 --> 00:48:57,883
[Dareum gasps]
[whoosh sound]

1001
00:48:57,950 --> 00:49:00,378
[Dareum laughs awkwardly]
If you wait over there,

1002
00:49:00,445 --> 00:49:02,444
I'll bring Koong out.

1003
00:49:02,511 --> 00:49:04,105
Okay.
[Dareum exhales]

1004
00:49:04,172 --> 00:49:06,767
I can't see anything right now.

1005
00:49:06,834 --> 00:49:08,183
[Dareum laughs awkwardly]
Right...

1006
00:49:13,138 --> 00:49:14,790
[Dareum grunts]
[music stops]

1007
00:49:14,857 --> 00:49:15,986
[relieved sigh]

1008
00:49:16,053 --> 00:49:17,826
That was the biggest crisis of my life.

1009
00:49:18,897 --> 00:49:20,126
[sighs]

1010
00:49:21,163 --> 00:49:22,639
[grunts]
[playful music]

1011
00:49:23,443 --> 00:49:25,138
I can't keep hiding the fact
[music stops]

1012
00:49:25,205 --> 00:49:27,138
that I'm Chan's fan...

1013
00:49:28,276 --> 00:49:29,238
Should I...

1014
00:49:30,019 --> 00:49:32,076
just tell him the truth?

1015
00:49:35,619 --> 00:49:36,857
[bells ringing]
[Dareum laughs]

1016
00:49:36,924 --> 00:49:38,680
[cat meowing]
(Hagi) They do seem
to recognize each other.

1017
00:49:38,747 --> 00:49:40,986
(Dareum) Right. Isn't that cool?

1018
00:49:41,053 --> 00:49:42,372
You said

1019
00:49:42,439 --> 00:49:44,872
they fought and stole each other's food
when they were together.

1020
00:49:47,009 --> 00:49:48,457
(Hagi) Fighting when you're together

1021
00:49:49,311 --> 00:49:50,593
and missing each other
when you're apart...

1022
00:49:52,818 --> 00:49:53,929
I guess it's the same

1023
00:49:55,655 --> 00:49:56,632
with people

1024
00:49:59,972 --> 00:50:01,071
and cats.

1025
00:50:01,138 --> 00:50:02,572
[laughs]
[cat meowing]

1026
00:50:08,580 --> 00:50:10,479
(Dareum) This is the perfect time.

1027
00:50:12,635 --> 00:50:14,149
(Dareum) Mr. Kang.

1028
00:50:15,454 --> 00:50:18,839
To be honest...

1029
00:50:20,092 --> 00:50:21,023
(Hagi) Yes?

1030
00:50:21,793 --> 00:50:23,825
[stammers]
Well...

1031
00:50:23,892 --> 00:50:26,865
[phone vibrating]
I've...

1032
00:50:26,932 --> 00:50:28,468
(Hagi) Just a moment.
[taps]

1033
00:50:30,869 --> 00:50:31,906
Hello.

1034
00:50:32,484 --> 00:50:35,304
I'm out right now,
so I'll check when I get home.

1035
00:50:36,172 --> 00:50:37,309
[call ending sound]

1036
00:50:37,376 --> 00:50:40,199
What were you saying?

1037
00:50:40,266 --> 00:50:41,176
(Dareum) What?

1038
00:50:41,913 --> 00:50:42,845
[grunts]

1039
00:50:43,912 --> 00:50:44,880
[laughs awkwardly]

1040
00:50:44,947 --> 00:50:48,217
I just wanted to thank you
for bringing Koong here.

1041
00:50:49,374 --> 00:50:51,453
(Hagi) I should be thanking you.

1042
00:50:52,378 --> 00:50:53,722
I got to see Jjak again

1043
00:50:54,693 --> 00:50:56,638
thanks to you.
[Dareum laughs]

1044
00:50:59,369 --> 00:51:00,672
And it's nice seeing you...

1045
00:51:03,498 --> 00:51:04,433
too.

1046
00:51:05,330 --> 00:51:06,830
[lively music]

1047
00:51:23,323 --> 00:51:25,005
Look at the time.

1048
00:51:25,072 --> 00:51:26,088
[Dareum reacts]

1049
00:51:26,155 --> 00:51:27,203
I should get going now.

1050
00:51:27,270 --> 00:51:28,772
That's so sudden.

1051
00:51:28,839 --> 00:51:29,594
[Dareum grunts]

1052
00:51:29,661 --> 00:51:32,038
(Hagi) Get some rest, Ms. Nam.
[Dareum reacts]

1053
00:51:32,105 --> 00:51:34,635
Bye, Koong.
[cat meowing]

1054
00:51:35,764 --> 00:51:37,299
I'll see you at work, then.

1055
00:51:37,366 --> 00:51:38,370
Right...

1056
00:51:38,437 --> 00:51:40,551
[door lock sound]
(Dareum) Get home safely, Mr. Kang!

1057
00:51:40,618 --> 00:51:41,706
(Hagi) Okay.

1058
00:51:41,773 --> 00:51:42,739
[door closes]

1059
00:51:43,375 --> 00:51:44,406
[door lock sound]

1060
00:51:50,967 --> 00:51:52,184
[music stops]

1061
00:51:53,802 --> 00:51:54,906
She must've understood, right?

1062
00:52:05,097 --> 00:52:06,472
(Hagi) And it's nice seeing you...

1063
00:52:06,539 --> 00:52:07,462
[whoosh sound]

1064
00:52:07,529 --> 00:52:08,572
too.

1065
00:52:08,639 --> 00:52:09,931
[whoosh sound]

1066
00:52:09,998 --> 00:52:11,472
Nice seeing you...

1067
00:52:12,871 --> 00:52:13,906
too...

1068
00:52:14,473 --> 00:52:16,056
[soft music]

1069
00:52:18,010 --> 00:52:19,006
Me too.

1070
00:52:23,548 --> 00:52:24,539
(Dareum) What?

1071
00:52:26,835 --> 00:52:28,084
No...

1072
00:52:28,151 --> 00:52:29,985
[Dareum grunts]
[music stops]

1073
00:52:30,052 --> 00:52:30,852
[hairdryer whirs]

1074
00:52:30,919 --> 00:52:32,824
[elegant music plays]
(Choi) Yes, it's her.

1075
00:52:32,891 --> 00:52:35,572
But how did you get photos
from the office?

1076
00:52:36,514 --> 00:52:38,127
[laughs]
Really?

1077
00:52:38,864 --> 00:52:39,995
That's no surprise.

1078
00:52:40,757 --> 00:52:42,197
Then I'll look forward to the article.

1079
00:52:44,264 --> 00:52:45,672
[call ending sound]
[taps]

1080
00:52:46,398 --> 00:52:47,536
[phone clunks]

1081
00:52:47,603 --> 00:52:48,804
[doorbell rings]
(Lee Chan, staff) Hello.

1082
00:52:48,871 --> 00:52:50,075
- (Wonbin) Hello.
- (staff) You're here.

1083
00:52:50,142 --> 00:52:51,672
- This way, please.
- (Lee Chan) Okay.

1084
00:52:54,546 --> 00:52:56,311
- (staff) We'll be ready for you soon.
- (Lee Chan) Okay.

1085
00:53:02,220 --> 00:53:05,457
(Choi) I heard you got cast
in Director Park Chandong's film.

1086
00:53:05,524 --> 00:53:06,889
Congratulations, Chan.

1087
00:53:07,790 --> 00:53:08,690
Thanks.

1088
00:53:10,908 --> 00:53:13,362
(Choi) I'm probably going to start
a global project as well.

1089
00:53:13,999 --> 00:53:15,063
I'm filming in the States too.

1090
00:53:17,018 --> 00:53:18,041
The States?

1091
00:53:18,108 --> 00:53:20,469
Yeah. Isn't that crazy timing?

1092
00:53:22,078 --> 00:53:25,207
(Choi) I guess we're meant
to keep running into each other.

1093
00:53:33,584 --> 00:53:34,752
[street sounds]
[elevator dings]

1094
00:53:34,819 --> 00:53:36,718
[elevator doors opening]
[Dareum, Yeongwoo laugh]

1095
00:53:36,785 --> 00:53:38,186
- (Dareum) They're so cute.
- (Yeongwoo) Yeah.

1096
00:53:38,253 --> 00:53:40,288
I could hardly sleep the last few days.
[button beeps]

1097
00:53:40,355 --> 00:53:41,705
They're so cute.

1098
00:53:41,772 --> 00:53:43,325
[thuds]
Oh, my gosh.

1099
00:53:43,392 --> 00:53:44,696
[whoosh sound]
[intriguing music]

1100
00:53:44,763 --> 00:53:46,428
- (Dareum) Mr. Kang.
- (Yeongwoo) Mr. Kang.

1101
00:53:49,668 --> 00:53:50,973
[taps]
[comical sound]

1102
00:53:51,470 --> 00:53:52,672
You're getting off work together?

1103
00:53:53,266 --> 00:53:56,655
(Dareum) Yes.
Mr. Park's coming to take the cats.

1104
00:53:56,722 --> 00:53:58,376
I was on my way out too.

1105
00:53:58,443 --> 00:54:00,006
We can go together.
[Dareum reacts]

1106
00:54:00,739 --> 00:54:01,613
[whoosh sound]
I'll give you a ride.

1107
00:54:01,680 --> 00:54:02,639
[Yeongwoo reacts]

1108
00:54:03,415 --> 00:54:04,412
(Hagi) It's on the way.

1109
00:54:04,479 --> 00:54:06,439
(Dareum) That's great.
[Dareum laughs]

1110
00:54:12,172 --> 00:54:13,438
[faint laugh]

1111
00:54:13,505 --> 00:54:14,539
[whoosh sound]

1112
00:54:16,285 --> 00:54:17,708
[spinning sound]

1113
00:54:17,775 --> 00:54:19,066
[whoosh sound]

1114
00:54:23,335 --> 00:54:24,600
[whoosh sound]

1115
00:54:27,970 --> 00:54:29,504
[sparkling sound]

1116
00:54:33,145 --> 00:54:34,172
[squeaking sound]

1117
00:54:36,782 --> 00:54:37,839
[whoosh sound]

1118
00:54:38,649 --> 00:54:39,681
[laughing sound]

1119
00:54:40,238 --> 00:54:41,283
[music stops]

1120
00:54:41,350 --> 00:54:42,554
[cat meowing]

1121
00:54:42,621 --> 00:54:46,405
Koong, Jjak, goodbye.

1122
00:54:47,092 --> 00:54:48,991
(Dareum) Don't forget me, okay?

1123
00:54:49,638 --> 00:54:50,938
[cat meowing continues]

1124
00:54:51,005 --> 00:54:52,305
Bye.

1125
00:54:52,772 --> 00:54:54,022
Bye.

1126
00:54:54,089 --> 00:54:55,063
[Yeongwoo clears throat]

1127
00:54:57,578 --> 00:55:00,272
(Yeongwoo) I'll take good care
of Koong and Jjak.

1128
00:55:00,339 --> 00:55:03,073
And Mr. Kang, thank you
for helping with the luggage.

1129
00:55:03,832 --> 00:55:05,674
- Right.
- (Dareum) Bye, Mr. Park.

1130
00:55:06,275 --> 00:55:09,114
By the way...
[cat meowing]

1131
00:55:09,181 --> 00:55:10,198
(Dareum) Yes?

1132
00:55:10,712 --> 00:55:12,647
It's nothing.
[Yeongwoo laughs]
[cheerful music]

1133
00:55:14,475 --> 00:55:16,147
I...

1134
00:55:18,620 --> 00:55:19,688
[Yeongwoo sighs]
[whoosh sound]

1135
00:55:19,755 --> 00:55:21,590
[Dareum laughs]
[drumroll sound]

1136
00:55:21,657 --> 00:55:23,159
[bell ringing sound]

1137
00:55:23,226 --> 00:55:26,029
[whoosh sound]
If you're not in a hurry to leave,

1138
00:55:26,096 --> 00:55:27,478
why don't we hang out a bit
as colleagues...

1139
00:55:27,545 --> 00:55:29,030
I mean, with Mr. Kang as well...
[claps]

1140
00:55:29,097 --> 00:55:30,098
How about some coffee?

1141
00:55:30,165 --> 00:55:31,703
[Dareum reacts]

1142
00:55:31,770 --> 00:55:32,906
(Hagi) Not today.

1143
00:55:33,498 --> 00:55:36,182
Cats can get really stressed
in an unfamiliar environment.

1144
00:55:36,249 --> 00:55:38,364
They should be with their guardian
on their first day.

1145
00:55:38,431 --> 00:55:40,046
[Dareum reacts]
(Yeongwoo) Oh, right.

1146
00:55:40,113 --> 00:55:42,171
Then I guess
we'll have to take a rain check.

1147
00:55:42,238 --> 00:55:44,161
Next time, then.
[Yeongwoo laughs]

1148
00:55:44,228 --> 00:55:46,618
(Hagi) You should hurry home
and help them settle down.
[music stops]

1149
00:55:46,685 --> 00:55:48,305
All right. I'll get going now!

1150
00:55:49,080 --> 00:55:50,185
(Dareum) Bye.

1151
00:55:52,124 --> 00:55:53,104
(Yeongwoo) Ms. Nam,

1152
00:55:53,171 --> 00:55:55,305
let's hang out together soon.
[Dareum laughs]

1153
00:55:55,372 --> 00:55:57,472
Without Mr. Kang.
[laughs]

1154
00:55:58,330 --> 00:56:00,247
Sure.
[door closes]

1155
00:56:00,314 --> 00:56:01,860
[car engine revs]

1156
00:56:04,331 --> 00:56:07,505
(Dareum) Take care, Koong, Jjak.

1157
00:56:08,907 --> 00:56:10,835
Take care of each other.
[Dareum sighs]

1158
00:56:14,732 --> 00:56:15,877
(Hagi) And don't fight.

1159
00:56:17,567 --> 00:56:18,826
[sniffles]

1160
00:56:18,893 --> 00:56:20,619
[lively music]
[Dareum grunts]

1161
00:56:20,686 --> 00:56:22,205
[Dareum sniffles and clears throat]

1162
00:56:23,322 --> 00:56:26,095
Ms. Nam, are you crying?

1163
00:56:26,162 --> 00:56:27,026
[Dareum grunts]

1164
00:56:27,093 --> 00:56:28,957
(Dareum) No.

1165
00:56:30,903 --> 00:56:33,372
I guess I've grown attached to them.

1166
00:56:38,737 --> 00:56:39,728
To be honest,

1167
00:56:41,312 --> 00:56:42,838
I feel like I've grown more attached.

1168
00:56:47,329 --> 00:56:49,872
I liked how you asked
if Koong ate well every day,

1169
00:56:51,982 --> 00:56:53,582
and I found myself looking forward

1170
00:56:55,894 --> 00:56:57,219
to your random photos.

1171
00:57:00,731 --> 00:57:01,690
Right.

1172
00:57:02,706 --> 00:57:03,992
Without them...

1173
00:57:06,906 --> 00:57:08,033
[laughs awkwardly]

1174
00:57:08,100 --> 00:57:09,539
there won't be a reason
to message you anymore.

1175
00:57:16,004 --> 00:57:16,939
(Hagi) I...

1176
00:57:22,210 --> 00:57:23,574
[stomach grumbling sound echoes]
[music fades]

1177
00:57:23,641 --> 00:57:25,213
[comical sound]

1178
00:57:26,091 --> 00:57:27,305
[Dareum exclaims]

1179
00:57:27,372 --> 00:57:29,851
[cheerful music]
[Dareum laughs]

1180
00:57:29,918 --> 00:57:31,920
What's wrong with my stomach?

1181
00:57:32,948 --> 00:57:34,346
[stomach grumbling]

1182
00:57:38,930 --> 00:57:40,095
Should we have dinner?

1183
00:57:41,680 --> 00:57:42,964
It'd be a shame to just go home.

1184
00:57:46,312 --> 00:57:49,337
[exclaims]
Sure. Sounds good.

1185
00:57:49,772 --> 00:57:51,306
(Hagi) Okay.
[Dareum laughs]

1186
00:57:51,373 --> 00:57:52,541
- Let's go.
- (Dareum) Okay.

1187
00:57:56,196 --> 00:57:57,405
[music stops]

1188
00:57:58,016 --> 00:57:59,538
(employee) Next party, please.

1189
00:57:59,605 --> 00:58:01,837
(Dareum) I really wanted to come here.

1190
00:58:01,904 --> 00:58:03,318
How did you know about this place?

1191
00:58:04,541 --> 00:58:05,587
(Hagi) Well...

1192
00:58:05,854 --> 00:58:06,497
(Kalguksu)

1193
00:58:06,521 --> 00:58:07,626
I heard this place was popular.

1194
00:58:07,693 --> 00:58:09,505
Yeah. It is.

1195
00:58:10,640 --> 00:58:12,063
[intriguing music]
(Dareum) We failed again.

1196
00:58:12,130 --> 00:58:15,263
[Mina groans]
When will we ever
get to try the kalguksu?

1197
00:58:15,330 --> 00:58:16,164
[Dareum sighs]

1198
00:58:16,231 --> 00:58:18,571
I really wanted to try that place.

1199
00:58:18,638 --> 00:58:20,502
- (Mina) Me too.
- Kalguksu?

1200
00:58:20,569 --> 00:58:21,503
[blip sound]

1201
00:58:21,570 --> 00:58:25,018
Kalguksu place nearby...
[typing sound]

1202
00:58:25,085 --> 00:58:28,079
[blip sound]
[beep sound]

1203
00:58:28,146 --> 00:58:29,339
(Kalguksu)
Found it.

1204
00:58:32,078 --> 00:58:34,073
[whoosh sound]
[customers murmuring]

1205
00:58:35,454 --> 00:58:37,100
You wanted to eat this that badly?

1206
00:58:37,167 --> 00:58:38,071
(Dareum) Yes!

1207
00:58:38,138 --> 00:58:41,039
It's really hard to eat here
since you can't make a reservation.

1208
00:58:42,670 --> 00:58:43,792
(customer 1) Over here!

1209
00:58:45,983 --> 00:58:47,499
[rustles]
[thuds]

1210
00:58:47,566 --> 00:58:49,172
(customer 2) Sorry.

1211
00:58:50,039 --> 00:58:51,166
[faint laugh]

1212
00:58:51,794 --> 00:58:53,071
Stand on this side, Ms. Nam.

1213
00:58:53,138 --> 00:58:54,906
(Dareum) Thank you.

1214
00:58:58,628 --> 00:58:59,946
[music stops]

1215
00:59:03,471 --> 00:59:04,505
[laughs awkwardly]

1216
00:59:06,612 --> 00:59:08,973
(employee) Two bowls of kalguksu.

1217
00:59:09,973 --> 00:59:12,143
- (Dareum) Thank you.
- (employee) Enjoy.

1218
00:59:12,210 --> 00:59:14,810
(Dareum) The soup looks so delicious.

1219
00:59:14,877 --> 00:59:16,672
I can already tell it'll be amazing.

1220
00:59:26,034 --> 00:59:27,872
[Hagi grunts]
What is it?

1221
00:59:27,939 --> 00:59:30,572
Is it not to your taste?

1222
00:59:32,811 --> 00:59:34,142
[slurps]

1223
00:59:39,684 --> 00:59:41,958
This is really tasty.

1224
00:59:42,025 --> 00:59:44,589
Right? I told you it'll be amazing!
[soft music]

1225
00:59:44,656 --> 00:59:46,372
[laughs]
Let's eat.

1226
00:59:49,689 --> 00:59:52,687
[slurps]

1227
00:59:53,372 --> 00:59:54,629
[Dareum exclaims]

1228
00:59:55,366 --> 00:59:56,868
[Dareum exclaims and claps]

1229
00:59:56,935 --> 00:59:58,572
(Dareum) It's really good.
[Hagi laughs]

1230
01:00:01,439 --> 01:00:02,604
(Dareum) That was so good.

1231
01:00:03,205 --> 01:00:05,010
It's really worth the wait, isn't it?

1232
01:00:05,077 --> 01:00:06,675
(Hagi) Yeah.
[music fades]

1233
01:00:08,780 --> 01:00:11,546
Mr. Kang, look.

1234
01:00:13,481 --> 01:00:14,728
(Dareum) Doesn't that look
exactly like Jjak?

1235
01:00:14,795 --> 01:00:17,252
[cat meowing sound]
That expression

1236
01:00:17,319 --> 01:00:20,839
and that tightly closed mouth.
It looks just like Jjak.
[laughs]

1237
01:00:20,906 --> 01:00:22,090
How cute!

1238
01:00:23,567 --> 01:00:24,893
- Should I get it for you?
- (Dareum) What?

1239
01:00:27,255 --> 01:00:29,231
Mr. Kang!
[music: "My Bias, My Boss" theme song]

1240
01:00:30,469 --> 01:00:31,705
[coin rattles]

1241
01:00:31,772 --> 01:00:32,934
[claw machine beeps]

1242
01:00:37,701 --> 01:00:38,879
[rattling]

1243
01:00:41,446 --> 01:00:42,948
[exclaims]

1244
01:00:43,015 --> 01:00:44,713
[coin rattles]
[claw machine beeps]

1245
01:00:45,922 --> 01:00:46,747
[sighs]

1246
01:00:46,814 --> 01:00:48,186
[coin rattles]
[claw machine beeps]

1247
01:00:48,253 --> 01:00:49,408
[sighs]

1248
01:00:51,615 --> 01:00:53,906
I got it! I...

1249
01:00:54,871 --> 01:00:56,247
[coin rattles]
[claw machine beeps]

1250
01:00:56,314 --> 01:00:57,572
[Dareum sighs]

1251
01:00:58,539 --> 01:00:59,594
[sighs]

1252
01:01:00,165 --> 01:01:01,730
[coin rattles]
[claw machine beeps]

1253
01:01:03,013 --> 01:01:04,632
[Hagi grunts]
[music stops]

1254
01:01:06,606 --> 01:01:08,670
[sighs]
Mr. Kang,

1255
01:01:08,737 --> 01:01:09,785
(Dareum) I think you've done enough.

1256
01:01:09,852 --> 01:01:12,452
I already had plenty of fun watching.

1257
01:01:12,519 --> 01:01:13,514
(Hagi) No.

1258
01:01:13,581 --> 01:01:14,805
I can see the pattern now.

1259
01:01:14,872 --> 01:01:15,810
(Dareum) What?

1260
01:01:17,439 --> 01:01:19,321
(Hagi) The claw's grip strength
is consistent,

1261
01:01:19,388 --> 01:01:22,250
but if you look closely,
it's slightly tilted to the left.

1262
01:01:22,317 --> 01:01:23,613
Just now,
[taps]

1263
01:01:24,389 --> 01:01:25,739
I got it from the wrong angle.

1264
01:01:26,739 --> 01:01:27,789
What...

1265
01:01:28,360 --> 01:01:32,103
Why are you so serious about winning that?

1266
01:01:34,096 --> 01:01:35,363
Well, I have a goal.

1267
01:01:36,021 --> 01:01:37,198
(Hagi) I have to get Jjak.

1268
01:01:37,766 --> 01:01:39,434
[cheerful music]
This will be my final try.

1269
01:01:41,006 --> 01:01:42,572
[coin rattles]
[claw machine beeps]

1270
01:01:42,639 --> 01:01:44,172
[scoffs]
[claw whirs]

1271
01:01:44,706 --> 01:01:45,740
(Hagi) Okay...

1272
01:01:46,408 --> 01:01:47,509
[Hagi grunts]

1273
01:01:48,039 --> 01:01:49,177
[claw machine stops]

1274
01:01:49,678 --> 01:01:50,616
[Hagi sighs]
[music stops]

1275
01:01:51,450 --> 01:01:52,881
[Dareum laughs]

1276
01:01:53,819 --> 01:01:55,073
[sighs]

1277
01:01:58,046 --> 01:02:01,996
(Dareum) Calculating the angle,
coming up with a strategy...

1278
01:02:02,063 --> 01:02:03,825
You were like a total pro.

1279
01:02:05,464 --> 01:02:07,572
(Hagi) I wanted to get you
the plushie that looked like Jjak.

1280
01:02:08,644 --> 01:02:10,865
- Sorry.
- (Dareum) Not at all!

1281
01:02:10,932 --> 01:02:12,902
This guy is cute too.

1282
01:02:12,969 --> 01:02:14,278
[laughs]

1283
01:02:14,345 --> 01:02:15,670
And so were you.

1284
01:02:16,541 --> 01:02:18,192
[lively music]

1285
01:02:19,678 --> 01:02:21,910
[baby laughing sound]

1286
01:02:26,922 --> 01:02:27,949
(Hagi) I...

1287
01:02:29,706 --> 01:02:30,982
had fun today.

1288
01:02:31,049 --> 01:02:32,087
[faint laugh]

1289
01:02:32,524 --> 01:02:33,488
Me too.

1290
01:02:34,219 --> 01:02:35,156
And...

1291
01:02:36,671 --> 01:02:37,992
even without Koong and Jjak,

1292
01:02:39,515 --> 01:02:40,729
(Hagi) you can still message me

1293
01:02:42,456 --> 01:02:43,531
without a particular reason.

1294
01:02:46,578 --> 01:02:47,535
I...

1295
01:02:48,376 --> 01:02:49,938
liked hearing from you

1296
01:02:52,413 --> 01:02:53,441
too.

1297
01:02:57,827 --> 01:02:58,880
[laughs awkwardly]

1298
01:03:06,921 --> 01:03:07,906
(Hagi) You know...

1299
01:03:10,129 --> 01:03:11,292
Not as the CEO,

1300
01:03:13,889 --> 01:03:15,130
but as just Kang Hagi...

1301
01:03:19,646 --> 01:03:22,711
I like...
[phone vibrating]
[music stops]

1302
01:03:26,214 --> 01:03:28,704
[phone continues vibrating]

1303
01:03:28,771 --> 01:03:29,605
[rustles]

1304
01:03:29,672 --> 01:03:30,750
Hang on.

1305
01:03:30,817 --> 01:03:31,746
[grunts]

1306
01:03:35,702 --> 01:03:38,906
[phone vibrating]

1307
01:03:42,820 --> 01:03:44,614
- Hey, Seula.
- (Seula) Hey!

1308
01:03:44,681 --> 01:03:45,431
This is crazy!

1309
01:03:45,455 --> 01:03:47,730
There's an article
about you and Chan dating!

1310
01:03:47,797 --> 01:03:49,269
[somber music]

1311
01:03:49,336 --> 01:03:52,272
There's even a photo of you on a date!

1312
01:03:54,512 --> 01:03:55,570
(Dareum) What?

1313
01:04:04,405 --> 01:04:05,982
(The two were seen on a late-night date,
chatting without a care for onlookers)

1314
01:04:06,006 --> 01:04:07,615
[whoosh sound]

1315
01:04:23,238 --> 01:04:24,365
Mr. Kang...

1316
01:04:24,970 --> 01:04:25,906
Is this...

1317
01:04:25,973 --> 01:04:27,035
[music stops]

1318
01:04:29,462 --> 01:04:30,538
true?

1319
01:04:32,641 --> 01:04:34,108
[calm music]

1320
01:04:35,614 --> 01:04:36,911
[sighs]

1321
01:05:03,521 --> 01:05:05,204
(Epilogue)
[writing sound]

1322
01:05:05,271 --> 01:05:06,407
[music stops]

1323
01:05:07,713 --> 01:05:08,843
(Lee Chan) Ms. Nam,

1324
01:05:09,533 --> 01:05:12,080
who are you more compatible with?
Him or me?

1325
01:05:17,616 --> 01:05:19,799
[music: "My Bias, My Boss" theme song]

1326
01:05:21,393 --> 01:05:22,790
[inhales]
I was just wondering...

1327
01:05:24,607 --> 01:05:26,871
if you're more drawn to one of us.
[writing sound]

1328
01:05:26,938 --> 01:05:27,966
(Koong, Jjak)
[ding sound]

1329
01:05:28,033 --> 01:05:29,797
(Hagi, Dareum)
[writing sound]

1330
01:05:30,311 --> 01:05:31,499
[sparkling sound]

1331
01:05:32,166 --> 01:05:33,638
[music: "My Bias, My Boss"
theme song continues]

1332
01:05:33,705 --> 01:05:36,405
(Hagi) You went on a date,
but you're not dating?

1333
01:05:37,305 --> 01:05:38,678
(vlogger) That's not a fan.
That's a total stalker right there.

1334
01:05:38,745 --> 01:05:41,765
- (fan) We're boycotting APPELLO!
- (fans) We're boycotting APPELLO!

1335
01:05:41,832 --> 01:05:43,396
(Wonbin) The CEO is away right now.

1336
01:05:43,463 --> 01:05:45,701
(Lee Chan) Dareum just got branded
as a stalker because of me.

1337
01:05:45,768 --> 01:05:47,396
(Dareum) There's nothing going on
between us,

1338
01:05:47,420 --> 01:05:48,653
despite what people think.

1339
01:05:48,720 --> 01:05:50,338
(Lee Chan) When I asked you
how you felt about Dareum,

1340
01:05:50,405 --> 01:05:51,786
did you answer me honestly?

1341
01:05:52,754 --> 01:05:54,088
(Hagi) Meet the reporter and settle this.

1342
01:05:54,679 --> 01:05:56,539
(Choi) You're doing this

1343
01:05:56,606 --> 01:05:58,091
just to protect one girl?

1344
01:05:58,158 --> 01:05:59,641
(Dareum) I won't resent you
if you fire me.

1345
01:05:59,665 --> 01:06:00,294
(Seula) Stop filming her!

1346
01:06:00,361 --> 01:06:02,307
(Minwoo) Do you really
have to go this far?

1347
01:06:02,374 --> 01:06:03,962
(Hagi) From now on...

1348
01:06:04,486 --> 01:06:08,286
I don't want to cause
further trouble for APPELLO.

